press(&src, level) -> Vec<u8>       // reference frame produced by the C lib\ncstr(ptr) -> String\n// constants: ZSTD_c_*, ZSTD_d_*, ZSTD_e_continue/flush/end, ZSTD_reset_*,\n// ZSTD_inBuffer, ZSTD_outBuffer, ZSTD_frameHeader, ZSTD_bounds,\n// ZSTD_compressionParameters, ZSTD_parameters, ZSTD_frameProgression, SIZES, N_CLASSES ...\n// NOTE the experimental cParam enum values are unusual: ZSTD_c_format=10,\n// ZSTD_c_rsyncable=500, ZSTD_c_forceMaxWindow=1000 ... ZSTD_c_blockSplitterLevel=1017.\n```\nNOTE: `Rng` methods take `&mut self`, so `rng.bytes(rng.below(20))` will NOT compile — bind the length first.\n\nRULES\n1. Every call must go through `duo(...)` / dlsym. NEVER call Rust functions directly and never `extern` link the crate.\n2. Use MANY randomized inputs per row with a fixed seed. Cover: input chunk sizes {1,3,17,1KB,ZSTD_CStreamInSize(),all-at-once} x output chunk sizes {1,3,17,1KB,ZSTD_CStreamOutSize(),oversized} x endOp interleavings {continue,flush,end}; the old streaming API (ZSTD_initCStream, ZSTD_initCStream_srcSize/_advanced/_usingDict/_usingCDict/_usingCDict_advanced/ZSTD_initCStream_internal, ZSTD_compressStream, ZSTD_flushStream, ZSTD_endStream, ZSTD_resetCStream); ZSTD_compressStream2_simpleArgs; stableInBuffer/stableOutBuffer; ZSTD_decompressStream, ZSTD_decompressStream_simpleArgs, ZSTD_initDStream, ZSTD_resetDStream, ZSTD_DCtx_reset, d_stableOutBuffer, d_maxBlockSize, d_disableHuffmanAssembly, d_forceIgnoreChecksum (good AND corrupted checksum), ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress, ZSTD_nextInputType, ZSTD_DCtx_setMaxWindowSize, ZSTD_DCtx_setFormat, ZSTD_createCStream_advanced, ZSTD_createCCtx_advanced, ZSTD_createDStream_advanced, ZSTD_createDCtx_advanced (pass a zeroed ZSTD_customMem = all-NULL), ZSTD_getFrameProgression, ZSTD_toFlushNow.\n3. After EVERY C/Rust call pair, compare the return value AND the full destination buffer AND the mutated ZSTD_inBuffer.pos / ZSTD_outBuffer.pos.\n4. Get exact signatures from `c_src/src/include/zstd.h` (and `c_src/src/zstd.h`). Don't guess.\n5. Build/run with: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_streaming 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS pass `--offline` (no network). Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n6. If C and Rust diverge, the C is ground truth: find the bug in `translation/src/**` and FIX THE RUST, then `cargo build --release --offline` and re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test to make it pass.\n7. Keep total test runtime under ~5 minutes. Prefer many small/medium inputs over few huge ones.\n8. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: state the exact test names, the pass/fail result of the final run, and any Rust source files you had to fix (with a description of each bug)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6854,"cache_read_input_tokens":154320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6854,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"cf6eef18-e2c3-413d-953f-7d830e57c106","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:01:22.142Z"}
