{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5jxhhozgjmqt4yjpamzb2ci5qgeh4iqrofzmxjdgfb3b3ufb7ghq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01QNGmzMsQon5cwJfWSkNsen","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B bufferless/block tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust translation differential test suite.\n\nWorking root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe\n- `c_src/` = original zstd 1.5.7 C source (READ ONLY, NEVER MODIFY). Built shared lib at `c_src/build/libzstd.so`.\n- `translation/` = the Rust crate (cdylib) under verification. Built at `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`.\n\nYOUR TASK: create `translation/tests/phase_b_bufferless.rs` covering rows 82-96 of `translation/CONFIGS.md` (read that file first, section \"Group 6 — bufferless / block-level API\"). It must load BOTH .so files via libloading and compare outputs byte-for-byte.\n\nHARNESS CONTRACT — `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already exists. READ IT FIRST. Do NOT modify it (other agents share it). If you need extra helpers, define them locally inside your own test file. Key API:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nlet (fc, fr) = duo::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(..) -> ..>(\"ZSTD_compressContinue\"); // dlsym in both libs\neqv(\"label\", c_value, rust_value);      // asserts equal\neqbuf(\"label\", &c_bytes, &r_bytes);     // asserts byte-identical\nlet ctx = CtxPair::cctx();              // ctx.c / ctx.r : *mut c_void, freed on drop\n                                        // also ::dctx() ::cstream() ::dstream() ::cctx_params()\nlet mut rng = Rng::new(seed);           // rng.next_u64/next_u32/below(n)/range(lo,hi)/byte/bytes(n)\nlet data = gen_class(class, size, seed); // class in 0..N_CLASSES\nis_err(n); c_compress(&src, level) -> Vec<u8>; cstr(ptr) -> String;\n// constants ZSTD_c_*, ZSTD_d_*, ZSTD_reset_*, structs ZSTD_inBuffer/ZSTD_outBuffer/\n// ZSTD_frameHeader/ZSTD_parameters/ZSTD_compressionParameters/ZSTD_frameParameters ...\n```\nNOTE: `Rng` methods take `&mut self`, so `rng.bytes(rng.below(20))` will NOT compile — bind the length first.\n\nCOVER these entry points (get exact signatures from `c_src/src/include/zstd.h`, the \"Buffer-less streaming compression/decompression\" and \"Block level API\" sections, plus `c_src/src/compress/zstd_compress_internal.h` and `c_src/src/decompress/zstd_decompress_internal.h` for the internal ones):\n- ZSTD_compressBegin, ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced, ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced_internal, ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict, ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict, ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_advanced, ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_deprecated\n- ZSTD_compressContinue, ZSTD_compressContinue_public, ZSTD_compressEnd, ZSTD_compressEnd_public, ZSTD_copyCCtx\n- ZSTD_decompressBegin, ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict, ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict, ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress, ZSTD_nextInputType, ZSTD_decompressContinue, ZSTD_copyDCtx\n- ZSTD_getBlockSize, ZSTD_compressBlock, ZSTD_compressBlock_deprecated, ZSTD_decompressBlock, ZSTD_decompressBlock_deprecated, ZSTD_insertBlock, ZSTD_checkContinuity, ZSTD_invalidateRepCodes, ZSTD_getcBlockSize, ZSTD_writeLastEmptyBlock\n- ZSTD_getSeqStore, ZSTD_resetSeqStore, ZSTD_reset_compressedBlockState, ZSTD_splitBlock, ZSTD_get1BlockSummary\n(For ZSTD_getSeqStore / ZSTD_get1BlockSummary just compare the returned scalar/summary values, or for pointer returns compare that both are non-NULL and compare the bytes they point at only if you can determine the exact struct layout from the C headers; if the layout is not fully determinable, restrict yourself to comparing the returned scalars and the observable compression output instead — do NOT guess a layout.)\n\nRULES\n1. Every call must go through `duo(...)` / dlsym. NEVER call Rust functions directly.\n2. Use MANY randomized inputs per row with a fixed seed: level grid (-5..22), all 9 strategies, input split into 1..N chunks of varying sizes, all 8 content classes, sizes crossing the 128KB block boundary, with and without dictionaries.\n3. After EVERY C/Rust call pair, compare the return value AND the destination buffer.\n4. Build/run with: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_bufferless 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS pass `--offline`. Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n5. If C and Rust diverge, the C is ground truth: find the bug in `translation/src/**` and FIX THE RUST, then `cargo build --release --offline` and re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test to make it pass.\n6. Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes.\n7. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: exact test names, pass/fail of the final run, and any Rust source files you fixed with a description of each bug."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3585,"cache_read_input_tokens":161174,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3585,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"df6ba39f-9524-48af-9b87-a8fffb11344d","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:01:44.462Z"}
