{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Etubxm8De8zLJ3CrmFViKC","type":"tool_result","content":"3004:  Use ZSTD_compressBegin(), or ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict() for dictionary compression.\n3006:  Then, consume your input using ZSTD_compressContinue().\n3008:  - ZSTD_compressContinue() has no internal buffer. It uses externally provided buffers only.\n3012:    ZSTD_compressContinue() doesn't guarantee recover after a failed compression.\n3013:  - ZSTD_compressContinue() presumes prior input ***is still accessible and unmodified*** (up to maximum distance size, see WindowLog).\n3015:  - ZSTD_compressContinue() detects that prior input has been overwritten when `src` buffer overlaps.\n3018:  Finish a frame with ZSTD_compressEnd(), which will write the last block(s) and optional checksum.\n3022:  `ZSTD_CCtx` object can be reused (ZSTD_compressBegin()) to compress again.\n3027:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressBegin(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, int compressionLevel);\n3029:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, int compressionLevel);\n3031:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, const ZSTD_CDict* cdict); /**< note: fails if cdict==NULL */\n3035:size_t ZSTD_copyCCtx(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, const ZSTD_CCtx* preparedCCtx, unsigned long long pledgedSrcSize); /**<  note: if pledgedSrcSize is not known, use ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN */\n3038:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressContinue(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);\n3040:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressEnd(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);\n3042:/* The ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced() and ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_advanced() are now DEPRECATED and will generate a compiler warning */\n3045:size_t ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced(ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize, ZSTD_parameters params, unsigned long long pledgedSrcSize); /**< pledgedSrcSize : If srcSize is not known at init time, use ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN */\n3048:size_t ZSTD_compressBegin_usingCDict_advanced(ZSTD_CCtx* const cctx, const ZSTD_CDict* const cdict, ZSTD_frameParameters const fParams, unsigned long long const pledgedSrcSize);   /* compression parameters are already set within cdict. pledgedSrcSize must be correct. If srcSize is not known, use macro ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN */\n3072:  ZSTD_decompressContinue() needs previous data blocks during decompression, up to `windowSize` bytes.\n3073:  ZSTD_decompressContinue() is very sensitive to contiguity,\n3081:  In a round buffer methodology, ZSTD_decompressContinue() decompresses each block next to previous one,\n3093:  Once buffers are setup, start decompression, with ZSTD_decompressBegin().\n3094:  If decompression requires a dictionary, use ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict() or ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict().\n3096:  Then use ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress() and ZSTD_decompressContinue() alternatively.\n3097:  ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress() tells how many bytes to provide as 'srcSize' to ZSTD_decompressContinue().\n3098:  ZSTD_decompressContinue() requires this _exact_ amount of bytes, or it will fail.\n3100:  result of ZSTD_decompressContinue() is the number of bytes regenerated within 'dst' (necessarily <= dstCapacity).\n3101:  It can be zero : it just means ZSTD_decompressContinue() has decoded some metadata item.\n3104:  A frame is fully decoded when ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress() returns zero.\n3107:  Note : it's possible to know if next input to present is a header or a block, using ZSTD_nextInputType().\n3119:  For skippable frames ZSTD_decompressContinue() always returns 0 : it only skips the content.\n3126:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_decompressBegin(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx);\n3127:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, const void* dict, size_t dictSize);\n3128:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDDict(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, const ZSTD_DDict* ddict);\n3130:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_nextSrcSizeToDecompress(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx);\n3131:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_decompressContinue(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);\n3135:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API void   ZSTD_copyDCtx(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, const ZSTD_DCtx* preparedDCtx);\n3136:typedef enum { ZSTDnit_frameHeader, ZSTDnit_blockHeader, ZSTDnit_block, ZSTDnit_lastBlock, ZSTDnit_checksum, ZSTDnit_skippableFrame } ZSTD_nextInputType_e;\n3137:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API ZSTD_nextInputType_e ZSTD_nextInputType(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx);\n3167:      + compression : any ZSTD_compressBegin*() variant, including with dictionary\n3168:      + decompression : any ZSTD_decompressBegin*() variant, including with dictionary\n3169:    - Block size is limited, it must be <= ZSTD_getBlockSize() <= ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX == 128 KB\n3173:    - When a block is considered not compressible enough, ZSTD_compressBlock() result will be 0 (zero) !\n3176:      + A block cannot be declared incompressible if ZSTD_compressBlock() return value was != 0.\n3178:      + ZSTD_decompressBlock() _doesn't accept uncompressed data as input_ !!\n3181:        Use ZSTD_insertBlock() for such a case.\n3186:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_getBlockSize   (const ZSTD_CCtx* cctx);\n3188:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_compressBlock  (ZSTD_CCtx* cctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);\n3190:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_decompressBlock(ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, void* dst, size_t dstCapacity, const void* src, size_t srcSize);\n3192:ZSTDLIB_STATIC_API size_t ZSTD_insertBlock    (ZSTD_DCtx* dctx, const void* blockStart, size_t blockSize);  /**< insert uncompressed block into `dctx` history. Useful for multi-blocks decompression. */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QNGmzMsQon5cwJfWSkNsen","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"59ab6bcb-ff01-4a73-8db5-5e112cd612f0","ti