{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cedsgkykvuu6nzw2tsqfnpyik6a4pkeo2veoe3q7qlppnm7jnzgq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01J98wxsynBZbjd3uLfRfYKs","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B legacy decoder tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust translation differential test suite.\n\nWorking root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe\n- `c_src/` = original zstd 1.5.7 C source (READ ONLY, NEVER MODIFY). Built shared lib at `c_src/build/libzstd.so`. Build config: ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5, XXH_NAMESPACE=ZSTD_, DYNAMIC_BMI2=0, no ZSTD_MULTITHREAD.\n- `translation/` = the Rust crate (cdylib) under verification. Built at `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`.\n\nYOUR TASK: create `translation/tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` covering rows 157-165 of `translation/CONFIGS.md` (read it first, \"Group 12 — legacy decoders v0.1 … v0.7\") AND row 166-168 style coverage is NOT yours.\n\nHARNESS CONTRACT — `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already exists. READ IT FIRST. Do NOT modify it (other agents share it). Define extra helpers locally in your own file. Key API:\n```rust\nmod common;\nuse common::*;\nlet (fc, fr) = duo::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(..) -> ..>(\"ZSTDv07_decompress\"); // dlsym in both libs\neqv(\"label\", c_value, rust_value); eqbuf(\"label\", &c, &r);\nlet mut rng = Rng::new(seed); let data = gen_class(class, size, seed);\nis_err(n); cstr(ptr); LEGACY_MAGICS (7 magic numbers, v0.1..v0.7)\n```\nNOTE: `Rng` methods take `&mut self`, so `rng.bytes(rng.below(20))` will NOT compile — bind the length first.\n\nThe legacy decoders are DECODE-ONLY: there is no legacy encoder in this library. So you cannot produce genuine v0.x frames. Therefore your strategy MUST be:\n(a) Enumerate ALL exported legacy symbols. Get the list with:\n    `nm -D --defined-only /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/c_src/build/libzstd.so | awk '{print $3}' | grep -E '^(ZSTDv0|ZBUFFv0|FSEv0|HUFv0)'`\n    Read `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_v01.h` .. `zstd_v07.h` and `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_legacy.h` for the exact signatures.\n(b) For every one of those symbols, call it in BOTH libraries with the same inputs and assert identical results. Use:\n    - random byte buffers of many sizes prefixed with each legacy magic number (these exercise the header parse + the error paths deterministically),\n    - structured pseudo-frames you build by hand from the legacy format (read the C decoder to work out what a minimally valid v0.x frame header looks like: magic + frame header byte(s) + block headers). Aim to get past the header into block decoding for at least the RAW and RLE block types of v0.4-v0.7.\n    - the streaming ZBUFFv0x_* APIs driven with many in/out chunk size combinations over those buffers.\n    - context lifecycle: createDCtx/freeDCtx/resetDCtx/sizeof where present, and decompressContinue/nextSrcSizeToDecompress loops.\n(c) Also test the dispatch path: ZSTD_decompress / ZSTD_decompressStream / ZSTD_isFrame / ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize / ZSTD_getFrameContentSize / ZSTD_decompressBound / ZSTD_getDictID_fromFrame on buffers starting with each of the 7 legacy magics (see `c_src/src/legacy/zstd_legacy.h` — only versions >= 5 are enabled by ZSTD_LEGACY_SUPPORT=5, so v0.1-v0.4 must be REJECTED identically by both, which is itself a required assertion).\n\nRULES\n1. Every call must go through `duo(...)` / dlsym. NEVER call Rust functions directly.\n2. MANY randomized inputs (fixed seed) per symbol — hundreds of buffers, not one.\n3. Compare return values AND full destination buffers AND any out-params.\n4. Build/run: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_legacy 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS pass `--offline`. Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n5. If C and Rust diverge, C is ground truth: fix `translation/src/legacy/**` (or wherever the bug is), `cargo build --release --offline`, re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test.\n6. Beware: feeding garbage to a legacy decoder may make the C library read out of bounds and segfault. That is a property of the C, not a bug to fix. If a specific input crashes BOTH libraries identically, drop that input from the suite and note it in your report. If it crashes only one, that IS a real divergence to fix in the Rust.\n7. Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: exact test names, pass/fail of the final run, the list of legacy symbols you exercised vs. any you could not, inputs you had to drop (with reason), and any Rust source files you fixed with a description of each bug."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3882,"cache_read_input_tokens":167433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3882,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"c29efcfd-da2b-440e-bbcc-9134b1b2930a","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:02:44.258Z"}
