e created by one library and must ONLY be passed to that same library. Always create a matching pair (one from the C .so, one from the Rust .so) and use each with its own library.\n\nCOVER (exact signatures from `c_src/src/include/zstd.h`):\nZSTD_createCDict, ZSTD_createCDict_byReference, ZSTD_createCDict_advanced, ZSTD_createCDict_advanced2, ZSTD_freeCDict, ZSTD_sizeof_CDict, ZSTD_getCParamsFromCDict, ZSTD_getDictID_fromCDict, ZSTD_compress_usingCDict, ZSTD_compress_usingCDict_advanced, ZSTD_CCtx_refCDict, ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary, ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary_byReference, ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary_advanced, ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix, ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix_advanced, ZSTD_createDDict, ZSTD_createDDict_byReference, ZSTD_createDDict_advanced, ZSTD_freeDDict, ZSTD_sizeof_DDict, ZSTD_DDict_dictContent, ZSTD_DDict_dictSize, ZSTD_copyDDictParameters, ZSTD_getDictID_fromDDict, ZSTD_DCtx_refDDict, ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary, ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary_byReference, ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary_advanced, ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix, ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix_advanced, ZSTD_decompress_usingDDict, ZSTD_getDictID_fromDict, ZSTD_getDictID_fromFrame, ZSTD_loadCEntropy, ZSTD_loadDEntropy, ZSTD_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary, ZSTD_estimateCDictSize_advanced, ZSTD_estimateDDictSize.\n\nConfiguration axes to cross-product:\n- dictLoadMethod {byCopy, byRef} x dictContentType {auto, rawContent, fullDict}\n- dict shapes: none, tiny (<8 bytes), raw random bytes, real trained dictionary produced by `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` (call it through the C .so to build the test fixture), dictionary with a corrupted magic\n- ZSTD_c_forceAttachDict {0,1,2,3} x srcSize {tiny, large} x strategy 1..9\n- ZSTD_c_enableDedicatedDictSearch {0,1} x strategy {greedy, lazy, lazy2}\n- ZSTD_c_prefetchCDictTables {auto,enable,disable}\n- ZSTD_c_deterministicRefPrefix {0,1} with refPrefix\n- ZSTD_d_refMultipleDDicts {single, multiple} with 1..4 DDicts\n- dictIDFlag {0,1} and every DID field width\n- For ZSTD_DDict_dictContent, compare the CONTENT BYTES pointed at (using ZSTD_DDict_dictSize), not the pointers.\n\nRULES\n1. Every call goes through `duo(...)` / dlsym. NEVER call Rust functions directly.\n2. MANY randomized inputs per row, fixed seed. Compare return values AND destination buffers AND round-trip correctness.\n3. Build/run: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_dict 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS `--offline`. Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n4. If C and Rust diverge, C is ground truth: fix `translation/src/**`, `cargo build --release --offline`, re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test.\n5. Known upstream C landmine (see \"Upstream C crashes\" in CONFIGS.md): calling `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams` with `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching=enable` but `ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch` unset divides by zero in the C. Avoid it. If you hit any other configuration that kills BOTH libraries identically, drop it and report it.\n6. Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: exact test names, pass/fail of the final run, any symbol you could not exercise (and why), and any Rust source files you fixed with a description of each bug.","uuid":"2934b488-d5b7-4434-9d11-6d52e6576d09","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a"}
