_displayLevel`, and `ZDICT_optimize*_cover` copies that global back into `parameters->zParams.notificationLevel`. Because libtest runs this binary's test fns on parallel threads in one process, a non-zero level in one test leaked into `row149_optimize_cover`'s out-param comparison (it observed C=1 / Rust=0 — a harness race, not a translation bug). `zdict.c` uses a local variable instead, so `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` (levels 0..4) and `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy` (levels 0..2) *are* exercised with non-zero levels in `row153_finalize_notification_levels`. Documented in a comment there.\n3. `nbThreads > 1` is not reachable: the C build has `ZSTD_MULTITHREAD` undefined (no `pthread_*` relocations in `c_src/build/libzstd.so`), which is also why `COVER_best_t`'s mutex/cond are plain `int` in the test's `#[repr(C)]` mirror (size asserted == 88 at compile time, alongside 12/48/56/16/24 for the other structs, cross-checked against the C build via ctypes).\n\nBonus: `COVER_warnOnSmallCorpus` (not on the required list) is also called in both libraries at `displayLevel` 0.\n\nNo files other than `translation/tests/phase_b_dictbuilder.rs` were created or modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":207802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_0136SfpGvNnN2Pyg2QB8qW4M","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"fdc1358c-e491-405f-a81d-5913ddec65bf","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:32:54.809Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B dictbuilder tests"}
