{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ej4jyw4vaaf6lt7u7doy47wfwiiwkblklbcyfv7u2se47mbvxhsa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Report\n\n**File created:** `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation/tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` (only file added; no Rust sources, `Cargo.toml`, `tests/common/mod.rs`, other test files, or `c_src/` were modified).\n\n**Final run:** `cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_legacy` → **32 passed, 0 failed, 1.90 s**.\n\n### Test names (all passing)\n`legacy_all_symbols_resolve_in_both_libraries`, `legacy_corpus_is_large`, `legacy_is_error_and_get_error_name`, `legacy_scalar_constants_and_ctx_sizes`, `legacy_v01_decoders`, `legacy_v02_decoders`, `legacy_v03_decoders`, `legacy_v04_decoders`, `legacy_v04_zbuff_streaming`, `legacy_v05_decoders`, `legacy_v05_advanced`, `legacy_v05_get_frame_params`, `legacy_v05_zbuff_streaming`, `legacy_v06_decoders`, `legacy_v06_advanced`, `legacy_v06_get_frame_params`, `legacy_v06_zbuff_streaming`, `legacy_v07_decoders`, `legacy_v07_advanced`, `legacy_v07_get_frame_params_and_decompressed_size`, `legacy_v07_zbuff_streaming`, `legacy_v07_checksummed_frames_streaming`, `legacy_crafted_frames_decode_to_known_output`, `legacy_fse_v05/06/07`, `legacy_huf_v05/06/07`, `dispatch_oneshot_on_legacy_magics`, `dispatch_stream_on_legacy_magics`, `dispatch_rejects_legacy_versions_below_five`.\n\n### Coverage\nAll **206** exported legacy symbols (`ZSTDv0*`, `ZBUFFv0*`, `FSEv0*`, `HUFv0*`) are called in both libraries with identical inputs — verified mechanically against `nm -D` output; none could not be exercised. (Note: `ZSTDv01_getDecompressedSize`, `ZSTDv02/03_decompressDCtx`, `ZSTDv04_isError` and `FSEv02/03/04`/`HUFv02/03/04` named in CONFIGS.md rows 158-161 are **not exported** — they are `static` in the C.)\n\nVolume: 720–977 hand-built/random buffers per version (~5 800 total) + 2 972 dispatch buffers, each crossed with 3–4 dst capacities, 10 in/out chunk shapes for ZBUFF, 5 for `ZSTD_decompressStream`. Return values, out-params, full DTables and destination buffers (with a 64 KB slack region appended so an over-write is also compared) are all diffed. Every driver carries a \"productive\" assertion so the suite fails if it degenerates into error-path-only coverage. `legacy_crafted_frames_decode_to_known_output` and `legacy_v07_checksummed_frames_streaming` additionally check against **ground truth**, not just C==Rust.\n\n### Divergences found / Rust files fixed\n**None.** C and Rust agreed on every input; no `translation/src/legacy/**` change was needed.\n\n### Inputs dropped (crash *both* libraries identically)\n1. `HUFv07_selectDecoder(dstSize == 0)` → **SIGFPE** (`cSrcSize*16/dstSize`); also `algoTime[Q]` OOB when `cSrcSize >= dstSize`. Domain restricted to the documented `0 < cSrcSize < dstSize <= 128 KB`.\n2. `ZSTDv07_freeDDict(NULL)` → **SIGSEGV** (dereferences `ddict->refContext` with no NULL check, unlike `ZSTDv07_freeDCtx`).\n3. `ZSTDv07_freeDCtx` on a `createDCtx_advanced(customMem)` context *after* `decompress_usingDDict`/`_usingPreparedDCtx` → glibc `free(): invalid pointer` abort, because `ZSTDv07_copyDCtx` memcpys the reference context's `customMem` over the caller's. The DDict path now uses a default-allocated context; the custom-allocator context is driven through `decompress_usingDict` instead.\n\n### Notable C behaviours pinned down while building the corpus\n- `bt_rle` is implemented **only** by v0.7's one-shot decoder; v0.1–v0.6 and v0.7's `decompressContinue` all `return ERROR(GENERIC)`.\n- A **zero-length RAW block** silently terminates a v0.1–v0.6 frame (`if (cBlockSize == 0) break;` instead of testing `bt_end`); v0.7 tests `bt_end` properly.\n- v0.7's frame checksum lives in the low 22 bits of the **end-block header** (`(XXH64(content,0) >> 11) & 0x3FFFFF`) and is verified only by the streaming decoders. Both correct and 1-bit-corrupted checksums are tested.\n- `common/mod.rs::LEGACY_MAGICS[0]` (`0x1EA92542`) is **not** the v0.1 magic — the real one is `0xFD2FB51E` read big-endian (bytes `FD 2F B5 1E`, LE `0x1EB52FFD`). I did not modify the shared harness; the test defines the correct magics locally and additionally feeds the harness list as extra garbage.\n\n### CONFIGS.md\nRows 157–165 ticked `[x]` with corrected/expanded descriptions. Three upstream-crash rows added to the \"Upstream C crashes\" table (now X3/X4/X5); a concurrently-added `ZSTD_compressSequences` row that had a duplicate `X2` id and sat outside the table was folded back in as X2 — its text is unchanged."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":946,"cache_read_input_tokens":304125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":946,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01J98wxsynBZbjd3uLfRfYKs","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"ac58ce4c-c41b-4f2c-af0c-e02e4a9d7108","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:33:40.372Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B legacy decoder tests"}
