{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_7uxt5emzotp2qrxqh4e33ehetzqztz6qmnk7tvdhcrlbdav7wqrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 20 tests pass. No divergence between the C and Rust libraries was found, so **no `translation/src/**` files needed changes**.\n\n## Deliverable\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation/tests/phase_b_dict.rs` (~2050 lines, new file; nothing else in the repo was modified).\n\nRun: `cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_dict` → **20 passed; 0 failed**, ~18 s wall.\n\n## Test names (final run: all `ok`)\n`row103_createCDict_compress_usingCDict`, `row104_createCDict_byReference`, `row105_createCDict_advanced_grid`, `row106_createCDict_advanced2_grid`, `row107_compress_usingCDict_advanced_fparams`, `row108_refCDict_forceAttachDict_strategies`, `row109_cctx_loadDictionary_repeated`, `row110_cctx_loadDictionary_byref_advanced`, `row111_cctx_refPrefix_deterministic`, `row112_createDDict_variants`, `row113_refDDict_multiple_ddicts`, `row114_dctx_loadDictionary_and_refPrefix`, `row115_getDictID_all_sources`, `row116_ddict_content_size_and_copyParams`, `row117_getCParamsFromCDict`, `row118_loadCEntropy_loadDEntropy`, `row119_dedicatedDictSearch_via_cdict`, `row119b_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary_direct`, `dict_size_estimates_and_sizeof`, `prefetchCDictTables_axis`.\n\n## Coverage\nAll 39 requested symbols are exercised through `duo()`/dlsym — none skipped.\n- Dict fixtures: none / tiny (3, 7 B) / raw random (16 B–10 KB) / text / zeros / two real `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` dictionaries (built through the C `.so`) / wrong-magic / truncated-trained; dictIDs patched to hit every DID field width (0, 1, 2, 4 bytes) incl. 0, 1, 255, 256, 65535, 65536, 0xFFFFFFFF.\n- Full `dictLoadMethod{byCopy,byRef} × dictContentType{auto,rawContent,fullDict}` cross-product on both the C- and D-side entry points; `forceAttachDict{0..3} × strategy 1..9 × srcSize{tiny,large}`; `enableDedicatedDictSearch{0,1} × strategy{greedy,lazy,lazy2,btlazy2-fallback}`; `prefetchCDictTables{auto,enable,disable}`; `deterministicRefPrefix{0,1}` with 8 prefix shapes; `refMultipleDDicts{single,multiple} × 1..4 DDicts × byCopy/byRef`; `dictIDFlag{0,1}`; `fParams` 8 combos; levels −5…22; the CONFIGS.md size ladder up to 1 MB.\n- `ZSTD_DDict_dictContent` compares the **content bytes** (via `ZSTD_DDict_dictSize`), never the pointers.\n- `ZSTD_loadCEntropy`/`ZSTD_loadDEntropy` compare the full output structs byte-for-byte (5632 B `ZSTD_compressedBlockState_t`, 27292 B `ZSTD_entropyDTables_t`; sizes probed with `offsetof`/`sizeof` on the real C headers), both buffers pre-zeroed so padding can't produce false mismatches.\n- `ZSTD_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary` is called **directly** (not just indirectly): the test declares a `#[repr(C)]` mirror of `ZSTD_MatchState_t` with static assertions pinning `size == 304` and the offsets the C build reports (`window.base` 8, `nextToUpdate` 44, `hashTable` 112, `chainTable` 128, `opt` 144, `cParams` 256), then compares the resulting hash/chain tables byte-for-byte over 9 param sets × 8 content classes × 4 sizes, with a non-vacuity assertion that the DDS table was actually filled.\n- `ZSTD_copyDDictParameters` is observed through a real `decompressBegin` + `nextSrcSizeToDecompress`/`decompressContinue` bufferless decode of a dict-compressed frame.\n\n## Two failures hit during development — both harness bugs, not translation bugs\n1. **Oversized decompression destination.** `ZSTD_decompress*` clobbers the unused tail of an oversized `dst` (`ZSTD_wildcopy`, up to the full remaining capacity — I confirmed the C itself writes past `produced+32`). Those bytes are outside the API contract. Fixed by decoding once into an **exactly-sized** buffer (whole buffer compared, strictest form) and once into a padded buffer where only the produced bytes are compared. No configuration was dropped.\n2. **`RLIMIT_DATA` on this host (6 GB) vs. parallel tests.** `ZSTD_createCDict(dict, 0, level)` has no srcSize hint and reserves the maximum window for the level — `ZSTD_estimateCDictSize(0, 22)` = **640 MB** (80 MB at 19, 160 at 20, 320 at 21); any `dictSize > 0` clamps it to < 1 MB. With 20 tests running concurrently in one process this exceeded the limit and one library returned `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` while the other succeeded (order-dependent, passed in isolation). Fixed by serializing only the `dictSize == 0 && level >= 10` cases behind a mutex (`BIG_CDICT`) — coverage unchanged.\n\n## Notes\n- No configuration killed both libraries; the documented X1 landmine was avoided (this file never calls `ZSTD_estimate*_usingCCtxParams`).\n- I did **not** tick rows 103–119 in `translation/CONFIGS.md`: other agents are editing that file concurrently and a whole-file rewrite could clobber their edits. All 17 rows now pass and can be marked `[x]`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":250,"cache_read_input_tokens":223948,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":250,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011dwFgnZ4wc3rtYdejgSN3w","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"bab83a05-fd23-4b2b-adb8-c4688fc59b46","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:35:30.565Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B dict tests"}
