{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a4a64bd945ee48b95","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_011dwFgnZ4wc3rtYdejgSN3w","status":"completed","output_file":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-agent-zaYAhA/tmp/claude-31072124/-local-home-scheschb--harvest-work-harvest-work-wA9tGe/b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a/tasks/a4a64bd945ee48b95.output","summary":"All 20 tests pass. No divergence between the C and Rust libraries was found, so **no `translation/src/**` files needed changes**.\n\n## Deliverable\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation/tests/phase_b_dict.rs` (~2050 lines, new file; nothing else in the repo was modified).\n\nRun: `cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_dict` → **20 passed; 0 failed**, ~18 s wall.\n\n## Test names (final run: all `ok`)\n`row103_createCDict_compress_usingCDict`, `row104_createCDict_byReference`, `row105_createCDict_advanced_grid`, `row106_createCDict_advanced2_grid`, `row107_compress_usingCDict_advanced_fparams`, `row108_refCDict_forceAttachDict_strategies`, `row109_cctx_loadDictionary_repeated`, `row110_cctx_loadDictionary_byref_advanced`, `row111_cctx_refPrefix_deterministic`, `row112_createDDict_variants`, `row113_refDDict_multiple_ddicts`, `row114_dctx_loadDictionary_and_refPrefix`, `row115_getDictID_all_sources`, `row116_ddict_content_size_and_copyParams`, `row117_getCParamsFromCDict`, `row118_loadCEntropy_loadDEntropy`, `row119_dedicatedDictSearch_via_cdict`, `row119b_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary_direct`, `dict_size_estimates_and_sizeof`, `prefetchCDictTables_axis`.\n\n## Coverage\nAll 39 requested symbols are exercised through `duo()`/dlsym — none skipped.\n- Dict fixtures: none / tiny (3, 7 B) / raw random (16 B–10 KB) / text / zeros / two real `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` dictionaries (built through the C `.so`) / wrong-magic / truncated-trained; dictIDs patched to hit every DID field width (0, 1, 2, 4 bytes) incl. 0, 1, 255, 256, 65535, 65536, 0xFFFFFFFF.\n- Full `dictLoadMethod{byCopy,byRef} × dictContentType{auto,rawContent,fullDict}` cross-product on both the C- and D-side entry points; `forceAttachDict{0..3} × strategy 1..9 × srcSize{tiny,large}`; `enableDedicatedDictSearch{0,1} × strategy{greedy,lazy,lazy2,btlazy2-fallback}`; `prefetchCDictTables{auto,enable,disable}`; `deterministicRefPrefix{0,1}` with 8 prefix shapes; `refMultipleDDicts{single,multiple} × 1..4 DDicts × byCopy/byRef`; `dictIDFlag{0,1}`; `fParams` 8 combos; levels −5…22; the CONFIGS.md size ladder up to 1 MB.\n- `ZSTD_DDict_dictContent` compares the **content bytes** (via `ZSTD_DDict_dictSize`), never the pointers.\n- `ZSTD_loadCEntropy`/`ZSTD_loadDEntropy` compare the full output structs byte-for-byte (5632 B `ZSTD_compressedBlockState_t`, 27292 B `ZSTD_entropyDTables_t`; sizes probed with `offsetof`/`sizeof` on the real C headers), both buffers pre-zeroed so padding can't produce false mismatches.\n- `ZSTD_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary` is called **directly** (not just indirectly): the test declares a `#[repr(C)]` mirror of `ZSTD_MatchState_t` with static assertions pinning `size == 304` and the offsets the C build reports (`window.base` 8, `nextToUpdate` 44, `hashTable` 112, `chainTable` 128, `opt` 144, `cParams` 256), then compares the resulting hash/chain tables byte-for-byte over 9 param sets × 8 content classes × 4 sizes, with a non-vacuity assertion that the DDS table was actually filled.\n- `ZSTD_copyDDictParameters` is observed through a real `decompressBegin` + `nextSrcSizeToDecompress`/`decompressContinue` bufferless decode of a dict-compressed frame.\n\n## Two failures hit during development — both harness bugs, not translation bugs\n1. **Oversized decompression destination.** `ZSTD_decompress*` clobbers the unused tail of an oversized `dst` (`ZSTD_wildcopy`, up to the full remaining capacity — I confirmed the C itself writes past `produced+32`). Those bytes are outside the API contract. Fixed by decoding once into an **exactly-sized** buffer (whole buffer compared, strictest form) and once into a padded buffer where only the produced bytes are compared. No configuration was dropped.\n2. **`RLIMIT_DATA` on this host (6 GB) vs. parallel tests.** `ZSTD_createCDict(dict, 0, level)` has no srcSize hint and reserves the maximum window for the level — `ZSTD_estimateCDictSize(0, 22)` = **640 MB** (80 MB at 19, 160 at 20, 320 at 21); any `dictSize > 0` clamps it to < 1 MB. With 20 tests running concurrently in one process this exceeded the limit and one library returned `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` while the other succeeded (order-dependent, passed in isolation). Fixed by serializing only the `dictSize == 0 && level >= 10` cases behind a mutex (`BIG_CDICT`) — coverage unchanged.\n\n## Notes\n- No configuration killed both libraries; the documented X1 landmine was avoided (this file never calls `ZSTD_estimate*_usingCCtxParams`).\n- I did **not** tick rows 103–119 in `translation/CONFIGS.md`: other agents are editing that file concurrently and a whole-file rewrite could clobber their edits. All 17 rows now pass and can be marked `[x]`.","usage":{"total_tokens":227308,"tool_uses":85,"duration_ms":1406793},"uuid":"7d86ecd8-b35d-4aa4-924e-af4c24962e42","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6krxzjgdkzj24jfgqiy2hc4etxv2hcqdbfvuo5yyuvw2inkvk7ea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/phase_b_entropy.rs` (4318 lines, 17 tests) is written and fully green.\n\n## Final run\n\n`cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_entropy` → **17 passed; 0 failed**, 28.4 s wall.\n\nTest names (all pass):\n`row126_xxh32_family`, `row127_xxh64_family`, `row128_hist`, `row131_135_fse_pipeline`, `row135_fse_errors_and_version`, `row136_huf_compress`, `row137_huf_decompress`, `row138_huf_tables`, `row139_zstd_build_fse_table`, `row140_zstd_decode_seq_headers`, `row141_zstd_compress_sequences`, `row142_zstd_literals_blocks`, `row143_zstd_compress_super_block`, `row144_select_block_compressor`, `row144_matchstate_table_builders`, `row145_all_block_compressors_e2e`, `row146_err_get_error_string`.\n\n## Rust source bugs found\n\n**None.** Every comparison (return values, full `count[]`/CTable/DTable/`ZSTD_seqSymbol`/hash-table/tag-table/chain-table/entropy-metadata buffers) matched byte-for-byte on the first passing run. No file under `translation/src/**` was modified; `Cargo.toml`, `tests/common/mod.rs` and other test files are untouched.\n\n## Symbols I could not exercise directly — and why\n\nRoughly half the names in the task list **do not exist in the zstd 1.5.7 build** (declared in headers only, or `static` in `legacy/`). Verified with `nm -D --defined-only` on both `.so` files, which export an *identical* 615-symbol set:\n\n- FSE: `FSE_compress`, `FSE_compress2`, `FSE_decompress`, `FSE_buildCTable`, `FSE_buildCTable_raw`, `FSE_buildDTable`, `FSE_buildDTable_raw`, `FSE_buildDTable_rle`, `FSE_decompress_usingDTable`, `FSE_decompress_wksp`, `FSE_count_simple`, `FSE_CTable_size`/`FSE_sizeof_CTable`/`FSE_DTable_size`. Only the 16 exported FSE entry points exist, and **all 16 are covered**.\n- HUF: `HUF_compress`, `HUF_compress2`, `HUF_compress4X_wksp`, `HUF_compress1X_wksp`, `HUF_decompress`, `HUF_decompress1X1`, `HUF_decompress1X1_DCtx`, `HUF_decompress1X2`, `HUF_decompress1X2_DCtx`, `HUF_decompress4X1(_DCtx/_usingDTable)`, `HUF_decompress4X2(_DCtx/_usingDTable)`, `HUF_decompress1X_DCtx`, `HUF_decompress4X_hufOnly`, `HUF_readDTableX1`, `HUF_readDTableX2`, `HUF_buildCTable`, `HUF_writeCTable`, `HUF_CTableBound` (a macro). **All 28 exported HUF entry points are covered**; the X1/X2 and 4X1/4X2 decoder bodies are reached through `HUF_decompress{1,4}X_usingDTable` fed with DTables built by `HUF_readDTableX1_wksp` / `HUF_readDTableX2_wksp`.\n- `ZSTD_compressBlock_deprecated` is exported but is the legacy `ZSTD_compressBlock()` entry point, not a matchfinder — left to the public-API test files. 41 (not 60) `ZSTD_compressBlock_*` symbols exist; they are driven end-to-end.\n\nEverything else is exercised directly, including the five low-level matchfinder helpers: I **did** safely build a mirrored `ZSTD_MatchState_t` (verified field-for-field against `zstd_compress_internal.h` and against the Rust translation's `repr(C)` struct) with 4x-oversized 64-byte-aligned hash/chain/tag tables, so `ZSTD_fillHashTable`, `ZSTD_fillDoubleHashTable`, `ZSTD_insertAndFindFirstIndex`, `ZSTD_row_update` and `ZSTD_updateTree` are called directly and their full table buffers compared (with non-vacuity assertions that the tables actually got populated).\n\n## Configurations deliberately excluded (C-side UB, documented in comments)\n\nThese crash or read out of bounds *in the C reference*, so they are outside the valid configuration surface:\n\n1. `FSE_optimalTableLog{,_internal}` / `FSE_normalizeCount` with `srcSize < 2` or `maxSymbolValue == 0` — both feed `ZSTD_highbit32(0)` (`bsr` on zero); C returned 5 vs. Rust 11 for `(0,1,0,0)`. Excluded, plus `maxSymbolValue == 0` skipped in the FSE pipeline (real zstd uses RLE there).\n2. `HIST_countFast{,_wksp}` / `HIST_count_simple` fed data outside `[0, maxSymbolValue]` — documented \"unsafe, won't check\"; `while (!count[maxSymbolValue]) maxSymbolValue--` underflows. Those three get alphabet-conforming input; `HIST_count{,_wksp}` still get raw data (and their `maxSymbolValue_tooSmall` error path is compared).\n3. `HUF_*` with an explicit `tableLog < HUF_minTableLog(cardinality)` — `HUF_setMaxHeight()` gets an impossible target and walks off its table. zstd only ever passes `HUF_TABLELOG_DEFAULT`.\n4. `ZSTD_buildFSETable` with `tableLog == 0` (i.e. `FSE_normalizeCount` returning \"single symbol\") — `1 << (tableLog-1)` underflows.\n\nNote: the C library is built with `-std=gnu99 -fPIC -w`, no `-DNDEBUG` and `DEBUGLEVEL=0`, so `assert()` is compiled out — which is why the above are hard crashes rather than assertion failures."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":153,"cache_read_input_tokens":299674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":153,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_017FJNQwSftAqpFARxzAhffw","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"16f3b37d-a548-4096-8b25-145835651603","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:35:40.037Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B entropy tests"}
