{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vqtl62cgvlul7mkcd7cyyoox2gwq2k4473223m5biybr6psy7roq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01GsrJW4SDePc8qy5zJVbJm3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase C entropy error tests","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are writing ONE Rust integration test file for a C-to-Rust translation differential test suite (Phase C = ERROR-PATH tests).\n\nWorking root: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe\n- `c_src/` = original zstd 1.5.7 C source (READ ONLY, NEVER MODIFY). Shared lib at `c_src/build/libzstd.so`.\n- `translation/` = the Rust crate (cdylib) under verification, at `translation/target/release/libzstd.so`.\n\nYOUR TASK: create `translation/tests/phase_c_entropy.rs`.\n\nIt must cover EVERY rejection site in these C files (read `translation/ERRORS.md`, sections for these files, and grep the C yourself to confirm):\n- `c_src/src/common/entropy_common.c` (14 sites)\n- `c_src/src/common/fse_decompress.c` (10 sites)\n- `c_src/src/common/bitstream.h` (4 sites)\n- `c_src/src/compress/fse_compress.c` (13 sites)\n- `c_src/src/compress/huf_compress.c` (17 sites)\n- `c_src/src/compress/hist.c` (5 sites)\n- `c_src/src/decompress/huf_decompress.c` (37 sites)\n\nFor each, construct the exact invalid input and assert the C and the Rust `.so` return the SAME error code / sentinel (use `FSE_isError`/`FSE_getErrorName`, `HUF_isError`/`HUF_getErrorName`, `ZSTD_getErrorCode`/`ZSTD_getErrorName` — compare the CODE, not just \"both failed\"). Triggers to construct include (non-exhaustive; derive the rest from the C):\n- `tableLog` above `FSE_MAX_TABLELOG` / `HUF_TABLELOG_MAX` -> `tableLog_tooLarge`\n- `maxSymbolValue` above `FSE_MAX_SYMBOL_VALUE` / 255 -> `maxSymbolValue_tooLarge`\n- `maxSymbolValue` too small for the data -> `maxSymbolValue_tooSmall`\n- `srcSize` 0 / 1 / oversized, `dstCapacity` 0 / 1 / one byte short -> `srcSize_wrong`, `dstSize_tooSmall`\n- corrupted normalized-count headers for `FSE_readNCount(_bmi2)` -> `corruption_detected`\n- corrupted Huffman weight tables for `HUF_readStats(_wksp)` / `HUF_readDTableX1_wksp` / `HUF_readDTableX2_wksp` -> `corruption_detected`\n- workspace buffers one byte too small for every `*_wksp` entry point -> `workSpace_tooSmall`\n- corrupted 1X/4X Huffman bitstreams for every `HUF_decompress*` variant (X1 and X2, 1X and 4X, `_usingDTable`, `_DCtx`, `_DCtx_wksp`, `_hufOnly(_wksp)`) -> `corruption_detected`\n- out-of-range `flags` bitmasks and out-of-range `HUF_repeat` enum values crossed over the FFI boundary\n- randomized corruption fuzzing (fixed seed, hundreds of mutations per shape) over valid FSE/HUF streams, comparing exact error codes\n\nHARNESS CONTRACT — `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already exists. READ IT FIRST. Do NOT modify it. Read `translation/tests/phase_c_decompress.rs` and `translation/tests/phase_c_params.rs` for the exact style, including the local `eqcode()` helper that compares error codes and names. Also read `translation/tests/phase_b_entropy.rs` (written by another agent) so you reuse its struct/table sizing knowledge and do NOT duplicate its happy-path coverage. Key API:\n```rust\nmod common; use common::*;\nlet (fc, fr) = duo::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(..) -> ..>(\"FSE_compress2\");\neqv(\"label\", c, r); eqbuf(\"label\", &c, &r); is_err(n); cstr(ptr);\nlet mut rng = Rng::new(seed); let d = gen_class(class, size, seed);\n```\n`Rng` methods take `&mut self`: `rng.bytes(rng.below(20))` will NOT compile — bind the length first.\n\nRULES\n1. Every call goes through `duo(...)`/dlsym. NEVER call Rust functions directly.\n2. Compare the returned error CODE, plus the destination buffer AND every out-param/table buffer in full.\n3. Build/run: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_c_entropy 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS `--offline`. Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n4. If C and Rust return different codes, C is ground truth: fix `translation/src/**`, `cargo build --release --offline`, re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test.\n5. Some C entry points have documented preconditions whose violation is UB and crashes BOTH libraries (e.g. `FSE_optimalTableLog`/`FSE_normalizeCount` with `srcSize < 2` or `maxSymbolValue == 0` reach `ZSTD_highbit32(0)`; `HIST_countFast*`/`HIST_count_simple` are documented \"unsafe, won't check\"; `HUF_*` with `tableLog < HUF_minTableLog(cardinality)` walks off a table; `HUF_selectDecoder(dstSize==0)` divides by zero). Stay inside the documented domain for those and LIST each exclusion in your report with the C evidence. Do not \"fix\" the Rust to match UB.\n6. Keep total runtime under ~5 minutes. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: exact test names, pass/fail of the final run, a mapping from ERRORS.md rejection sites to the test that triggers them (note any site you could NOT reach and why), and any Rust source files you fixed with a description of each bug."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":440690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1292,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"286641f6-598d-4413-8acd-70b15c20d5c7","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:37:53.469Z"}
