n27\t| `contentSizeFlag` | 0,1 | frame header `FCS` field size (0/1/2/4/8 bytes) |\n28\t| `checksumFlag` | 0,1 | XXH64 trailer + `ZSTD_error_checksum_wrong` |\n29\t| `dictIDFlag` | 0,1 | frame header DID field |\n30\t| `nbWorkers` | 0 (only value the non-MT build accepts) | `ZSTD_c_nbWorkers` |\n31\t| `enableLongDistanceMatching` | auto0/1/2 (`ZSTD_ps_auto/enable/disable`) | `ZSTD_ldm_*` |\n32\t| `ldmHashLog`,`ldmMinMatch`,`ldmBucketSizeLog`,`ldmHashRateLog` | bounds per `getBounds` | `ZSTD_ldm_adjustParameters` |\n33\t| `format` (exp2) | `ZSTD_f_zstd1`0, `ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless`1 | frame header write/read |\n34\t| `forceMaxWindow` (exp3) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_d_windowLogMax` interaction |\n35\t| `forceAttachDict` (exp4) | `ZSTD_dictDefaultAttach`0, `ForceAttach`1, `ForceCopy`2, `ForceLoad`3 | `ZSTD_resetCCtx_usingCDict` 3-way |\n36\t| `literalCompressionMode` (exp5) | auto0/huffman1/uncompressed2 | `ZSTD_compressLiterals` |\n37\t| `srcSizeHint` (exp7) | 0, small, large | `ZSTD_getCParamsFromCCtxParams` |\n38\t| `enableDedicatedDictSearch` (exp8) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_dedicatedDictSearch_lazy_loadDictionary` |\n39\t| `stableInBuffer` (exp9) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_compressStream2` buffer bypass |\n40\t| `stableOutBuffer` (exp10) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_compressStream2` buffer bypass |\n41\t| `blockDelimiters` (exp11) | `ZSTD_sf_noBlockDelimiters`0, `ZSTD_sf_explicitBlockDelimiters`1 | `ZSTD_compressSequences` |\n42\t| `validateSequences` (exp12) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_validateSequence` |\n43\t| `splitAfterSequences` (exp13) | auto0/enable1/disable2 | `ZSTD_preSplitBlock` |\n44\t| `useRowMatchFinder` (exp14) | auto0/enable1/disable2 | `ZSTD_selectBlockCompressor` row variants |\n45\t| `deterministicRefPrefix` (exp15) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix` window handling |\n46\t| `prefetchCDictTables` (exp16) | auto0/enable1/disable2 | `ZSTD_resetCCtx_byAttachingCDict` |\n47\t| `enableSeqProducerFallback` (exp17) | 0,1 | external sequence producer |\n48\t| `repcodeResolution` (exp19) | auto0/enable1/disable2 | `ZSTD_compressSequences` |\n49\t| `blockSplitterLevel` (exp20) | 0..6 (`ZSTD_BLOCKSPLITTER_LEVEL_MAX`) | `ZSTD_splitBlock` |\n50\t| `rsyncable` (exp1) | 0,1 | MT-only, still a settable/gettable param |\n51\t| `overlapLog`,`jobSize` | bounds per `getBounds` | MT params, still settable |\n52\t\n53\t### Decompression-parameter axes (`ZSTD_d_*`)\n54\t\n55\t| axis | values | branch |\n56\t|---|---|---|\n57\t| `windowLogMax` | 10..31 | `ZSTD_error_frameParameter_windowTooLarge` |\n58\t| `format` (exp1) | `ZSTD_f_zstd1`, `ZSTD_f_zstd1_magicless` | `ZSTD_getFrameHeader_advanced` |\n59\t| `stableOutBuffer` (exp2) | 0,1 | `ZSTD_decompressStream` output bypass |\n60\t| `forceIgnoreChecksum` (exp3) | `ZSTD_d_validateChecksum`0, `ZSTD_d_ignoreChecksum`1 | checksum verify |\n61\t| `refMultipleDDicts` (exp4) | `ZSTD_rmd_refSingleDDict`0, `ZSTD_rmd_refMultipleDDicts`1 | DDict hash set |\n62\t| `disableHuffmanAssembly` (exp5) | 0,1 | `HUF_decompress` (C build has no asm → both identical) |\n63\t| `maxBlockSize` (exp6) | 0, 1024..131072 | block size validation |\n64\t\n65\t### Dictionary axes\n66\t\n67\t| axis | values | branch |\n68\t|---|---|---|\n69\t| entry point | `ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary` / `_byReference` / `_advanced`, `ZSTD_CCtx_refPrefix(_advanced)`, `ZSTD_CCtx_refCDict`, `ZSTD_compress_usingDict`, `ZSTD_compress_usingCDict(_advanced)`, `ZSTD_compressBegin_usingDict/usingCDict(_advanced)`, `ZSTD_initCStream_usingDict/usingCDict(_advanced)` | — |\n70\t| `ZSTD_dictLoadMethod_e` | `byCopy`0, `byRef`1 | `ZSTD_CDict`/`ZSTD_DDict` init |\n71\t| `ZSTD_dictContentType_e` | `dct_auto`0, `dct_rawContent`1, `dct_fullDict`2 | `ZSTD_loadCEntropy`/`ZSTD_loadDEntropy` |\n72\t| dict shape | none, raw random bytes, real trained dict (`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer`), dict with wrong magic, tiny dict (<8B) | — |\n73\t| decode side | `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary(_byReference/_advanced)`, `ZSTD_DCtx_refDDict`, `ZSTD_DCtx_refPrefix(_advanced)`, `ZSTD_decompress_usingDict`, `ZSTD_decompress_usingDDict`, `ZSTD_initDStream_usingDict/usingDDict`, `ZSTD_decompressBegin_usingDict/usingDDict` | — |\n74\t\n75\t### Input-shape axes\n76\t\n77\t`empty(0)`, `1`, `7`, `128`, `1KB`, `8KB`, `64KB`, `128KB-1`, `128KB`, `128KB+1`\n78\t(block boundary), `256KB`, `1MB`, `>window` — crossed with content classes:\n79\t`zeros`, `single repeated byte`, `2-byte pattern`, `incompressible random`,\n80\t`text-like (low-entropy alphabet)`, `long-range duplicated blocks (LDM bait)`,\n81\t`RLE-able runs`, `already-compressed data`.\n82\t\n83\t### Streaming-shape axes\n84\t\n85\tinput chunk size ∈ {1, 3, 17, 1KB, `ZSTD_CStreamInSize()`, all-at-once},\n86\toutput chunk size ∈ {1, 3, 17, 1KB, `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize()`, oversized},\n87\t`ZSTD_EndDirective` ∈ {`continue`0, `flush`1, `end`2} in every interleaving.\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t## Upstream C crashes (configurations excluded from the differential suite)\n91\t\n92\tA few configurations make the **C** library itself die, so no differential\n93\tcomparison is possible (the process is gone before a value can be returned).\n94\tThey are recorded here rather than silently dropped.\n95\t\n96\t| # | entry point | configuration | what the C does |\n97\t|---|-------------|---------------|-----------------|\n98\t| X1 | `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams` / `ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize_usingCCtxParams` | a bare `ZSTD_CCtx_params` with `ZSTD_c_enableLongDistanceMatching = ZSTD_ps_enable` and `ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch` left at its default 0 | reaches `ZSTD_ldm_getMaxNbSeq()` -> `maxChunkSize / params.minMatchLength` with `minMatchLength == 0` (`ZSTD_ldm_adjustParameters()` has not run yet) and dies with **SIGFPE** (integer divide by zero). `translation/src/compress/zstd_ldm.rs::ZSTD_ldm_getMaxNbSeq` transliterates the same division, so the Rust also aborts. Not differentiable; the tests always set `ZSTD_c_ldmMinMatch` when they enable LDM on a params object. |\n99\t| X2 | `ZSTD_compressSequences` | any valid `(inSeqs, src)` pair with `dstCapacity` smaller than the frame needs (measured with `dstCapacity` = 10 while 18 bytes were needed) | writes **70 bytes *below* `dst`** and *then* returns `ZSTD_error_dstSize_tooSmall`. The Rust port reproduces the same pointer arithmetic and scribbles the same bytes in the same place. The test keeps this row differential by giving both destinations a 64 KiB canary guard band on each side and comparing the whole padded region (`tests/phase_b_sequences.rs::row122_compress_sequences`). |\n100\t| X3 | `HUFv07_selectDecoder` | `dstSize == 0` | computes `cSrcSize * 16 / dstSize` and dies with **SIGFPE**. Documented contract is `0 < cSrcSize < dstSize <= 128 KB`; outside it `algoTime[Q]` is also indexed out of bounds. `tests/phase_b_legacy.rs` restricts the domain accordingly. |\n101\t| X4 | `ZSTDv07_freeDDict` | `ddict == NULL` | dereferences `ddict->refContext->customMem` without a NULL check and **segfaults**. Unlike `ZSTDv07_freeDCtx`, NULL is not supported. Not exercised. |\n102\t| X6 | `COVER_computeEpochs` | `nbDmers == 0` | `epochs.size = MIN(k*10, nbDmers) == 0`, then `nbDmers / epochs.size` -> **SIGFPE**. COVER/FASTCOVER never call it that way (`*_ctx_init` guarantees >= 1 dmer). `tests/phase_b_dictbuilder.rs` excludes it. |\n103\t| X5 | `ZSTDv07_freeDCtx` after `ZSTDv07_decompress_usingDDict` / `_usingPreparedDCtx` on a context built by `ZSTDv07_createDCtx_advanced(customMem)` | any | `ZSTDv07_copyDCtx()` memcpys the *reference* context over `dctx`, including its `customMem`, so the context is later released with the reference's `free` instead of the caller's — glibc aborts with `free(): invalid pointer`. The tests use a default-allocated context for the DDict path. |\n104\t\n105\t## C preconditions that are UB when violated (excluded)\n106\t\n107\t| # | entry point | precondition | what the C does when violated |\n108\t|---|-------------|--------------|-------------------------------|\n109\t| P1 | `ZSTD_selectBlockCompressor` | `zstd_compress.c`: *\"assumption : strat is a valid strategy\"*; `dictMode` in `[0,3]` | indexes `blockCompressor[dictMode][strat]` / `rowBasedBlockCompressors[dictMode][strat-ZSTD_greedy]` with no validation -> out-of-bounds *read*, silently returning a garbage function pointer. Rust's bounds-checked indexing panics instead. Precondition violation, not a translation difference; `tests/phase_c_params.rs` probes only the documented domain. |\n110\t| P2 | `ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter`, `ZSTD_CCtxParams_getParameter` | non-NULL params object | dereferences `CCtxParams` immediately (`zstd_compress.c:770`) with no NULL check, unlike `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init` which does `RETURN_ERROR_IF(!cctxParams, GENERIC, ...)`. NULL segfaults the C. Excluded; the checked `_init` / `_init_advanced` NULL paths *are* tested. |\n111\t| P3 | `ZSTD_decompressBlock`, `ZSTD_decompressBlock_deprecated` | `zstd.h`: the block API is *\"not protected against malicious input\"* | fully random block payloads can drive out-of-bounds accesses. `tests/phase_c_decompress.rs` restricts the block-level fuzz accordingly. |\n112\t\n113\t## Unspecified C values (fields excluded from comparison)\n114\t\n115\t| # | entry point | what is unspecified |\n116\t|---|-------------|---------------------|\n117\t| U2 | any decoder entry point that returns an error mid-frame (`ZSTD_decompress`, `ZSTD_decompressDCtx`, `ZSTD_decompressStream`, `ZSTD_decompressContinue`) | `ZSTD_execSequence()` performs an unconditional 16-byte `ZSTD_copy16(op, *litPtr)` even when `litLength < 16`. For a frame whose literals were staged into `dctx->litBuffer`, up to 14 bytes of **never-written `litBuffer`** are copied into `dst` before the following offset check returns `corruption_detected`. With a heap-allocated DCtx those bytes are whatever `malloc` last left there, so they differ between the two libraries purely because of allocation history. **Verified not a translation difference**: driven through `ZSTD_initStaticDCtx` / `ZSTD_initStaticDStream` over a workspace pre-filled with 0x11 / 0x22 / 0x00, the C and the Rust `.so` emit byte-identical output (the fill byte) in every case. `tests/phase_c_decompress.rs` therefore runs every context-based decode on a static workspace with the same fill in both libraries, which makes the error-path partial output fully specified and comparable; only the self-allocating `ZSTD_decompress()` skips the `dst` comparison on the error path. |\n118\t| U1 | `ZSTD_get1BlockSummary` | on its error path the C does `BlockSummary bs; bs.nbSequences = ERROR(externalSequences_invalid); return bs;` (`zstd_compress.c:7462`) and returns `bs.blockSize` / `bs.litSize` **uninitialised**. Only `nbSequences` is observable; the Rust zero-initialises the other two fields. |\n119\t\n120\t---\n121\t\n122\t## Rows\n123\t\n124\tLegend: `[x]` = passes across randomized inputs (both `.so`s byte-identical).\n125\t\n126\t### Group 1 — version / bounds / pure helpers (`tests/phase_b_core.rs`)\n127\t\n128\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n129\t|---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|\n130\t| 1 | `ZSTD_versionNumber`, `ZSTD_versionString` | no input | [ ] |\n131\t| 2 | `ZSTD_maxCLevel`, `ZSTD_minCLevel`, `ZSTD_defaultCLevel` | no input | [ ] |\n132\t| 3 | `ZSTD_compressBound` | srcSize = 0,1,…,1MB, `ZSTD_MAX_INPUT_SIZE`, huge | [ ] |\n133\t| 4 | `ZSTD_decompressBound` | valid 1..8-frame streams + truncated + garbage | [ ] |\n134\t| 5 | `ZSTD_isError`, `ZSTD_getErrorCode`, `ZSTD_getErrorName`, `ZSTD_getErrorString` | every code 0..130 and every `(size_t)-n` | [ ] |\n135\t| 6 | `ZSTD_cParam_getBounds` | all 20 public params + all 19 experimental params + invalid ints | [ ] |\n136\t| 7 | `ZSTD_dParam_getBounds` | `d_windowLogMax` + exp1..exp6 + invalid ints | [ ] |\n137\t| 8 | `ZSTD_getCParams` | level ∈ min..22 × srcSizeHint ∈ {0,unknown,1,1K,1M,1G} × dictSize ∈ {0,1K,1M} | [ ] |\n138\t| 9 | `ZSTD_getParams` | same cross-product as row 8 | [ ] |\n139\t| 10 | `ZSTD_adjustCParams` | all cParams grids × srcSize/dictSize grid | [ ] |\n140\t| 11 | `ZSTD_checkCParams` | all cParams grids (valid + boundary) | [ ] |\n141\t| 12 | `ZSTD_cycleLog` | hashLog 0..31 × all 9 strategies | [ ] |\n142\t| 13 | `ZSTD_CStreamInSize`, `ZSTD_CStreamOutSize`, `ZSTD_DStreamInSize`, `ZSTD_DStreamOutSize` | no input | [ ] |\n143\t| 14 | `ZSTD_sizeof_CCtx/CDict/CStream/DCtx/DDict/DStream` | fresh, after use, after dict load | [ ] |\n144\t| 15 | `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize`, `_usingCParams`, `_usingCCtxParams` | level grid × cParams grid | [ ] |\n145\t| 16 | `ZSTD_estimateCStreamSize`, `_usingCParams`, `_usingCCtxParams` | level grid × cParams grid | [ ] |\n146\t| 17 | `ZSTD_estimateDCtxSize`, `ZSTD_estimateDStreamSize`, `_fromFrame` | windowSize grid, real frames | [ ] |\n147\t| 18 | `ZSTD_estimateCDictSize`, `_advanced` | dictSize grid × level × dictLoadMethod | [ ] |\n148\t| 19 | `ZSTD_estimateDDictSize` | dictSize grid × dictLoadMethod | [ ] |\n149\t| 20 | `ZSTD_getBlockSize`, `ZSTD_decodingBufferSize_min`, `ZSTD_decompressionMargin`, `ZSTD_sequenceBound` | windowSize/blockSize grid, real frames | [ ] |\n150\t\n151\t### Group 2 — one-shot compress / decompress (`tests/phase_b_core.rs`)\n152\t\n153\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n154\t|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n155\t| 21 | `ZSTD_compress` + `ZSTD_decompress` | level ∈ {min,-5..-1,0,1..22} × all 13 input sizes × all 8 content classes | [ ] |\n156\t| 22 | `ZSTD_compressCCtx` + `ZSTD_decompressDCtx` | same grid, context reused across calls | [ ] |\n157\t| 23 | `ZSTD_compress` | dstCapacity exactly `compressBound`, exactly the compressed size, one byte less | [ ] |\n158\t| 24 | `ZSTD_compress2` (default params) | same grid as row 21 | [ ] |\n159\t| 25 | `ZSTD_findFrameCompressedSize`, `ZSTD_findDecompressedSize`, `ZSTD_getFrameContentSize`, `ZSTD_getDecompressedSize` | 1..8 concatenated frames, with/without contentSize, with/without checksum, with skippable frames interleaved | [ ] |\n160\t| 26 | `ZSTD_getFrameHeader`, `ZSTD_getFrameHeader_advanced` | every FCS field width (0/1/2/4/8), every DID width (0/1/2/4), single-segment, checksum on/off, magicless | [ ] |\n161\t| 27 | `ZSTD_frameHeaderSize` | all header shapes of row 26 | [ ] |\n162\t| 28 | `ZSTD_isFrame`, `ZSTD_isSkippableFrame` | zstd frames, skippable magics `0x184D2A50..5F`, legacy magics, random | [ ] |\n163\t| 29 | `ZSTD_writeSkippableFrame`, `ZSTD_readSkippableFrame` | magicVariant 0..15 × payload sizes 0..1K | [ ] |\n164\t| 30 | `ZSTD_compress_usingDict`, `ZSTD_decompress_usingDict` | dict ∈ {raw, trained, none} × dictSize grid × level grid | [ ] |\n165\t\n166\t### Group 3 — `ZSTD_CCtx` parameter cross-product (`tests/phase_b_params.rs`)\n167\t\n168\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n169\t|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n170\t| 31 | `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` + `ZSTD_CCtx_getParameter` | every param × {min, min+1, mid, max-1, max} — get-back value must match | [ ] |\n171\t| 32 | `ZSTD_CCtx_setParameter` + `compressStream2` + roundtrip | `strategy` 1..9 × `minMatch` 3..7 × `windowLog` {10,17,23} | [ ] |\n172\t| 33 | same | `strategy` 1..9 × `useRowMatchFinder` {auto,enable,disable} | [ ] |\n173\t| 34 | same | `strategy` 1..9 × `targetLength` {0,16,64,999,131072} | [ ] |\n174\t| 35 | same | `hashLog`×`chainLog`×`searchLog` grid (valid combos only) × strategy | [ ] |\n175\t| 36 | same | `contentSizeFlag`×`checksumFlag`×`dictIDFlag` = 8 combos × pledgedSrcSize {unknown, exact} | [ ] |\n176\t| 37 | same | `format` {zstd1, magicless} × checksum {0,1} × contentSize {0,1} | [ ] |\n177\t| 38 | same | `enableLongDistanceMatching` {auto,enable,disable} × `ldmHashLog`×`ldmMinMatch`×`ldmBucketSizeLog`×`ldmHashRateLog` grid, LDM-bait input ≥ 1MB | [ ] |\n178\t| 39 | same | `literalCompressionMode` {auto,huffman,uncompressed} × content classes | [ ] |\n179\t| 40 | same | `targetCBlockSize` {0,1340,4096,65536,131072} × input ≥ 256KB (super-block path) | [ ] |\n180\t| 41 | same | `maxBlockSize` {0,1024,4096,65536,131072} × input ≥ 256KB | [ ] |\n181\t| 42 | same | `blockSplitterLevel` 0..6 × `splitAfterSequences` {auto,enable,disable} × mixed-entropy input | [ ] |\n182\t| 43 | same | `srcSizeHint` {0,1,1K,1M,1G} × real srcSize {1K,1M} | [ ] |\n183\t| 44 | same | `forceMaxWindow` {0,1} × `windowLog` {10,17,27} × decoder `windowLogMax` {10,17,27,31} | [ ] |\n184\t| 45 | same | `rsyncable` {0,1}, `jobSize` grid, `overlapLog` grid, `nbWorkers`=0 (non-MT build) | [ ] |\n185\t| 46 | same | `deterministicRefPrefix` {0,1} × `refPrefix` | [ ] |\n186\t| 47 | same | `prefetchCDictTables` {auto,enable,disable} × CDict | [ ] |\n187\t| 48 | same | `enableDedicatedDictSearch` {0,1} × strategy {greedy,lazy,lazy2} × CDict | [ ] |\n188\t| 49 | same | `validateSequences` {0,1} (valid sequences only) | [ ] |\n189\t| 50 | same | `enableSeqProducerFallback` {0,1} with no producer registered | [ ] |\n190\t| 51 | same | `repcodeResolution` {auto,enable,disable} | [ ] |\n191\t| 52 | `ZSTD_CCtx_setCParams`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setFParams`, `ZSTD_CCtx_setParams` | full struct grids | [ ] |\n192\t| 53 | `ZSTD_CCtx_reset` | `ZSTD_reset_session_only`/`parameters`/`session_and_parameters` at every point in a session | [ ] |\n193\t| 54 | `ZSTD_CCtx_setPledgedSrcSize` | exact, unknown(0/`ZSTD_CONTENTSIZE_UNKNOWN`), and > actual? (see ERRORS) | [ ] |\n194\t| 55 | `ZSTD_getFrameProgression`, `ZSTD_toFlushNow` | sampled at every step of a streaming session, all 9 strategies | [ ] |\n195\t| 56 | `ZSTD_CCtx_trace` | called with a NULL-hook build (always NULL) | [ ] |\n196\t\n197\t### Group 4 — `ZSTD_CCtx_params` object (`tests/phase_b_params.rs`)\n198\t\n199\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration | [ ] |\n200\t|---|----------------|---------------|-----|\n201\t| 57 | `ZSTD_createCCtxParams`/`ZSTD_freeCCtxParams`/`ZSTD_CCtxParams_reset` | fresh + after set | [ ] |\n202\t| 58 | `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init` | every level in min..22 | [ ] |\n203\t| 59 | `ZSTD_CCtxParams_init_advanced` | full `ZSTD_parameters` grid |