ccel` = 0 or above 10, `nbThreads` > 1 in a non-MT build, `shrinkDictMaxRegression` out of range\n- `ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_*` with parameter combinations it rejects\n- `ZDICT_finalizeDictionary` with a customDictContent bigger than the dict buffer, `dictContentSize` = 0, a corrupt/oversized `ZDICT_params_t`\n- `ZDICT_getDictID` / `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize` on buffers that are too short, have the wrong magic, or have a corrupt header -> `dictionary_corrupted`\n- `ZSTD_createDDict*` / `ZSTD_initStaticDDict` with a corrupt dictionary, a dictionary shorter than 8 bytes, workspace too small, NULL inputs -> `dictionary_corrupted` / NULL returns\n- `ZSTD_DDict_dictContent` / `_dictSize` / `ZSTD_copyDDictParameters` / `ZSTD_getDictID_fromDDict` on every failure shape you can legally construct\n- randomized corruption fuzzing (fixed seed, hundreds of mutations) of a real `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer` dictionary, fed to `ZSTD_createDDict`, `ZSTD_CCtx_loadDictionary`, `ZSTD_DCtx_loadDictionary`, `ZSTD_getDictID_fromDict`, `ZDICT_getDictID`, `ZDICT_getDictHeaderSize`, comparing exact error codes\n\nHARNESS CONTRACT — `translation/tests/common/mod.rs` already exists. READ IT FIRST. Do NOT modify it. Read `translation/tests/phase_c_decompress.rs` and `translation/tests/phase_c_params.rs` for the exact style, including the local `eqcode()` helper that compares error codes AND names. Also read `translation/tests/phase_b_dictbuilder.rs` (another agent wrote it) to reuse its `#[repr(C)]` struct mirrors and size assertions, and to avoid duplicating its happy-path coverage. Key API:\n```rust\nmod common; use common::*;\nlet (fc, fr) = duo::<unsafe extern \"C\" fn(..) -> ..>(\"ZDICT_trainFromBuffer\");\neqv(\"label\", c, r); eqbuf(\"label\", &c, &r); is_err(n); cstr(ptr);\nlet mut rng = Rng::new(seed); let d = gen_class(class, size, seed);\n```\n`Rng` methods take `&mut self`: `rng.bytes(rng.below(20))` will NOT compile — bind the length first.\n\nRULES\n1. Every call goes through `duo