turned error CODE, plus the destination buffer AND the in/out `parameters` struct in full.\n3. Build/run: `cd /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation && timeout 600 cargo test --offline --release --test phase_c_dictbuilder 2>&1 | tail -40`. ALWAYS `--offline`. Iterate until it compiles and ALL tests pass.\n4. If C and Rust return different codes, C is ground truth: fix `translation/src/dictbuilder/**` (or wherever), `cargo build --release --offline`, re-run. NEVER modify c_src/ and NEVER weaken a test.\n5. KNOWN upstream landmine (see the \"Upstream C crashes\" table in `translation/CONFIGS.md`): `COVER_computeEpochs(_, nbDmers = 0, _, _)` divides by zero -> SIGFPE. Avoid it. `notificationLevel > 0` on the COVER/FASTCOVER trainers writes to a process-global `g_displayLevel` that leaks across libtest's parallel threads — keep it at 0 for those two families. If you find a NEW configuration that kills BOTH libraries identically, drop it and report it with C evidence.\n6. Dictionary training is slow: keep sample corpora small and total runtime under ~5 minutes.\n7. Do not modify Cargo.toml, tests/common/mod.rs, or any other test file.\n\nFINAL REPORT: exact test names, pass/fail of the final run, a mapping from ERRORS.md rejection sites to the test that triggers them, any site you could NOT reach and why, and any Rust source files you fixed with a description of each bug.","uuid":"cc62bbff-4f5d-4eaf-a3d9-4841175db2ae","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a"}
