{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_khpjkcxrzkff3g2hyfgsh2jv2vkgbnubdbj4zhluhxrudiqcoz2a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-wA9tGe/translation/tests/phase_b_bufferless.rs` (2527 lines) covers CONFIGS.md rows 82–96.\n\n## Final run\n\n`cd translation && cargo test --offline --release --test phase_b_bufferless` → **16 passed, 0 failed, ~25 s** (verified stable over 5 consecutive runs; also re-ran `phase_a_smoke` (4 ok) and `phase_b_core` (24 ok) to confirm nothing else regressed).\n\nTest names:\n`row82_compress_begin_continue_end`, `row83_compress_begin_advanced`, `row83b_compress_begin_advanced_internal`, `row84_compress_begin_using_dict_and_cdict`, `row85_compress_continue_end_public`, `row86_copy_cctx`, `row87_decompress_bufferless`, `row88_decompress_begin_using_dict`, `row89_copy_dctx`, `row90_block_api`, `row91_insert_block_and_repcodes`, `row92_getc_block_size`, `row93_write_last_empty_block`, `row94_block_internals`, `row95_seq_store`, `row96_split_block_and_block_summary`.\n\nAll 34 required entry points are exercised via `duo()`/dlsym only, over the level ladder (-5..22), all 9 strategies, all 8 content classes, sizes 0…1 MB crossing the 128 KB boundary, 1..6-chunk splits, and none/raw/trained/CDict/DDict dictionaries with every `dictLoadMethod`×`dictContentType`.\n\n## Rust source files fixed\n**None** — no C/Rust divergence was found. Every mismatch I hit turned out to be a defect in my own test's assumptions, not in `translation/src/**`. I did not weaken any comparison of defined outputs; instead I bounded the comparisons to what the C API actually defines:\n\n1. `SeqStore_t.sequences`/`.lit` are NULL until a block actually reaches the match finder (`compressBegin` only sets the capacities), so the deep array comparison is gated on both builds reporting the same null-ness; `maxNbSeq/maxNbLit/longLengthType/longLengthPos` plus the sequence and literal byte arrays are still compared. A `deep > 50` counter guards against the test going vacuous.\n2. `ZSTD_get1BlockSummary`'s error path leaves `blockSize`/`litSize` as uninitialised stack slots in the C, so only `nbSequences` is compared there (full struct on success).\n3. `ZSTD_copyDCtx` does not copy `headerBuffer` (it stops at `&dctx->inBuff`), so a mid-frame hand-over is only valid at step 0 or at a block boundary — both builds returned the same \"Unknown frame descriptor\" for the invalid case.\n4. The decoder legitimately uses the tail of `dst` as literals scratch plus up to `WILDCOPY_OVERLENGTH` slop past the output, so buffer comparisons are limited to `[0, produced)`. To keep this from hiding a real bug I added 64 guard bytes past `dstCapacity` in row94 and assert **neither** build writes outside the buffer it was handed (it does not).\n5. My first `ZSTD_decompressBlock_internal` call passed a `dst` unrelated to the context's history (that function does no continuity check of its own), producing wild match reads; it now decodes into the buffer the context's `virtualStart`/`prefixStart` already point at.\n6. A trained dictionary forced to `ZSTD_dct_rawContent` loses its dictID, so those frames correctly fail to decode; asserted as an expected failure rather than success.\n\n## One environment note worth passing on\nThe process has `RLIMIT_DATA = 6 GB` and a level-22 `ZSTD_CCtx` costs 705 MB (`ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize(22)`), so 16 tests running in parallel each holding ultra-level contexts exhausted the heap: the Rust `ZSTD_compressBegin` returned `(size_t)-64` = `ZSTD_error_memory_allocation` while the C one had already succeeded, and elsewhere the process took SIGSEGV. That was pure memory pressure, not a translation bug. The test now keeps ultra levels (20–22) with unknown pledged size confined to one short section of `row82` (fresh pair created and dropped per case), caps other tests at level 17/19, and reaches the ultra *strategies* (incl. `btultra2`) cheaply via `ZSTD_compressBegin_advanced` with `ZSTD_getParams(lvl, realSrcSize, 0)` so the window — and hence the workspace — stays small. Other Phase-B test files that use levels 20–22 in many parallel tests may hit the same ceiling."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":189,"cache_read_input_tokens":253235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":189,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01QNGmzMsQon5cwJfWSkNsen","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"1c61df43-182a-461f-b582-b03de837e8c9","timestamp":"2026-09-04T05:50:11.568Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B bufferless/block tests"}
