opagated in `err_cover_optimize_rejections` |\n| 479, 480, 481 (`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_cover`) | `err_cover_train_rejections`, `err_cover_fastcover_param_grid` |\n| 483 (`COVER_checkTotalCompressedSize` GENERIC), 484 (`COVER_best_finish` GENERIC) | `err_cover_internal_generic_paths` |\n| 485 (`COVER_tryParameters` GENERIC, observable) | `err_cover_optimize_rejections` |\n| 486, 487, 488, 489 (`ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_cover`) | `err_cover_optimize_rejections`, `err_cover_fastcover_param_grid` |\n| 492, 493 (`divsufsort`/`divbwt` `return -1`) | `err_divsufsort_bad_arguments` |\n| 494, 495 (`FASTCOVER_ctx_init` srcSize_wrong) | `err_fastcover_ctx_init_rejections`, `err_fastcover_optimize_rejections` |\n| 499 (`FASTCOVER_tryParameters` GENERIC, observable) | `err_fastcover_optimize_rejections`, `err_zdict_train_from_buffer_wrapper` |\n| 500, 501, 502 (`ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_fastCover`) | `err_fastcover_train_rejections`, `err_cover_fastcover_param_grid` |\n| 503–507 (`ZDICT_optimizeTrainFromBuffer_fastCover`) | `err_fastcover_optimize_rejections`, `err_cover_fastcover_param_grid`, `err_zdict_train_from_buffer_wrapper` |\n| 305, 306, 307 (`ZSTD_loadEntropy_intoDDict` corrupted) | `err_ddict_create_advanced`, `err_dictionary_corruption_fuzz` |\n| 308 (`ZSTD_initDDict_internal` memory_allocation) | `err_ddict_create_advanced` (failure-injecting `ZSTD_customMem`: 1st alloc succeeds, 2nd returns NULL) |\n| 309, 310, 311 (`ZSTD_createDDict_advanced` NULL) | `err_ddict_create_advanced` |\n| 312, 313, 314 (`ZSTD_initStaticDDict` NULL) | `err_init_static_ddict` |\n| `ZSTD_DDict_dictContent`/`_dictSize`/`ZSTD_copyDDictParameters`/`ZSTD_getDictID_fromDDict` | `err_ddict_copy_parameters_and_accessors` |\n\nNotable techniques: row 514 is reached by handing `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer` a `dictContentSize` whose low 32 bits + 128 KB set bit 31 (the check fires before any read); row 516 by first *measuring* the exact entropy-header size, then re-running with `maxDstSize` equal to it so all four tables fit but the 12 rep-offset bytes do not; rows 483/484/485/499 by supplying an unsatisfiable `samplesSizes[0]` / `selection.dictSize` / `dictBufferCapacity` so the internal `malloc` fails.\n\n### Sites NOT reached (with C evidence, documented in the file header)\n- **All `ERROR(memory_allocation)` in `dictBuilder/**`** — rows 478, 482, 490, 491, 497, 498, 508, 509, 511, 512, 515, 520, 526. They need `malloc`/`calloc` to return NULL and the dictBuilder API has no allocator hook; the host has 371 GB RAM with `vm.overcommit_memory=0`, so no legal-size allocation fails. `POOL_create` additionally *cannot* fail here: `common/pool.c:326-336` (`#else /* ZSTD_MULTITHREAD not defined */`) unconditionally returns `&g_poolCtx`, so `nbThreads > 1` never yields `memory_allocation` — a differential probe with `nbThreads ∈ {0,1,2,8,u32::MAX}` is included instead.\n- **Rows 477 / 496** (`nbTestSamples < 1`) — `nbTrainSamples = (unsigned)((double)nbSamples*splitPoint)` under `splitPoint < 1.0`. For every double `sp < 1.0`, the exact product `N·sp` is more than half an ULP below `N`, so it never rounds up to `N`; small `sp` hits `nbTrainSamples < 5` first.\n- **Row 519** (`hSize + minContentSize > dictBufferCapacity`) — needs an entropy header ≥ 249 bytes while `HBUFFSIZE` caps it at 256 and `dictBufferCapacity ≥ 256` is enforced one line earlier. ~5000 randomized configurations (sample content class, count, size, compression level −9…22, dictContentSize) driven against the C build produced a maximum header of **198** bytes. The same statement family in `ZDICT_analyzeEntropy` (row 516) *is* covered.\n- **Row 522** — dead code: the only exported entry point `ZDICT_trainFromBuffer_legacy` (zdict.c:1091) already `return 0;` for `sBuffSize < ZDICT_MIN_SAMPLES_SIZE` before calling the static `_unsafe_legacy`. The `return 0` sentinel is covered instead.\n- **Rows 513, 523, 525** — \"should never happen\" guards; `divsufsort` can only return `-2` (malloc) inside `ZDICT_trainBuffer_legacy` since `T`/`SA` are non-NULL and `n ≥ 0`.\n\n### Rust source files fixed\n**None.** Every probe already agreed bit-for-bit between `c_src/build/libzstd.so` and `translation/target/release/libzstd.so` — return code, `ZSTD_getErrorCode`, `ZSTD_getErrorName`, `ZDICT_getErrorName`, `ZDICT_isError`, the full destination buffer, and the full in/out `parameters` struct (`splitPoint` compared by bit pattern so NaN round-trips are checked exactly).\n\n### Newly found upstream C landmines (avoided, not added to CONFIGS.md since I was told not to modify other files)\n- `ZDICT_addEntropyTablesFromBuffer(buf, dictContentSize, cap, …)` with a `dictContentSize` whose low 32 bits + 128 KB do **not** set bit 31 (e.g. `0xFFFF_FFFF`, `1<<40`) passes the `offcodeMax > 30` guard and then `XXH64`s `dictContentSize` bytes out of bounds → SIGSEGV in **both** libraries identically. The test only uses values that trip the guard.\n- `COVER_map_init(map, size)` computes `map->sizeLog = ZSTD_highbit32(size) + 2` then `(U32)1 << sizeLog`; for `k - d + 1 ≥ 2^30` that is a shift by ≥ 32 (C UB; x86 masks the count, and Rust release-mode masks identically). Requires a ≥ 1 GiB `dictBufferCapacity`, so it is not exercised."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_read_input_tokens":254466,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":592,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01WCZHz6uac4djVtvVUhM9QX","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"5b569439-02f3-4f89-bea2-b67328c32125","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:06:16.625Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C dictbuilder+legacy errors"}
