{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ensht5ybspjdnuljzdyoe34fczfq64aghzabamthibnmn43fddkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/tests/phase_c_entropy.rs` (4651 lines, 36 tests) — **final run: 36 passed, 0 failed, 3.57 s**.\n\n## Test names and ERRORS.md row mapping\n\n**`common/bitstream.h` (rows 1-4)**\n| row | test |\n|---|---|\n| 1 `BIT_initCStream` dstSize_tooSmall | `err_bit_initcstream_dstsize_toosmall` — error is *swallowed* by `FSE_compress_usingCTable_generic` (L565), so only observable as a `0` return; asserted for every `dstCapacity <= 8` |\n| 2 srcSize_wrong / 3 GENERIC / 4 corruption_detected | `err_bit_initdstream_all_three` (via `HUF_decompress1X_usingDTable`: srcSize 0; last byte 0 with srcSize ≥ 8; last byte 0 with srcSize < 8) |\n\n**`common/entropy_common.c` (rows 5-18)**\n| rows | test |\n|---|---|\n| 5 | `err_fse_readncount_short_header_corruption` (truncated valid header, `countSize > hbSize`) |\n| 6 | `err_fse_readncount_tablelog_toolarge` (byte-0 low nibble 11-15) |\n| 7, 9 | `err_fse_readncount_remaining_corruption` |\n| 8 | `err_fse_readncount_maxsymbolvalue_toosmall` — witness `[0xF0,0x03,0…]`, `*maxSVPtr = UINT_MAX` (the *only* way to exit with `remaining==1 && charnum>maxSV1`) |\n| 10-18 | `err_huf_readstats_targeted` (one targeted input per site: srcSize 0; special-header truncation; `oSize>=hwSize`; FSE-header truncation; weight 13-15; all-zero weights; `[12,12]`; `[12,1]`; `[2,2]`/`[2,1,1,1]`) |\n| + wksp | `err_huf_readstats_wksp_toosmall` (bisected threshold, one byte short → GENERIC; just-short-of-DTable → tableLog_tooLarge) |\n| fuzz | `err_fse_readncount_fuzz`, `err_huf_readstats_fuzz` |\n\n**`common/fse_decompress.c` (rows 24-33)**\n`err_fse_builddtable_wksp_guards` (24, 25, 26) · `err_fse_builddtable_wksp_generic` (27) · `err_fse_decompress_wksp_guards` (28, 29/30, 31, 32, 33) · `err_fse_decompress_wksp_fuzz`\n\n**`compress/fse_compress.c` (rows 46-58)**\n`err_fse_buildctable_wksp_tablelog_toolarge` (46) · `err_fse_writencount_all` (47/48/50/52 dstSize_tooSmall via a full `dstCapacity` sweep on a sparse distribution with a 254-symbol zero run so the `symbol>=start+24` skip fires; 49 `remaining<1`; 51 `remaining!=1`; 53; 54) · `err_fse_normalizecount_guards` (56, 57, 58) · `err_fse_normalizem2_generic` (55) · `err_fse_optimaltablelog_domain`\n\nRow 55 required a brute-forced witness: `FSE_normalizeCount(norm, tableLog=6, count=[2482120768, 3880001444], total=2^32+545, msv=1, useLowProbCount=1)`. It is reachable only because `ZSTD_div64(..., (U32)total)` truncates `total`, making `count[s]*rStep` wrap 2^64 so `sEnd-sStart == 0`.\n\n**`compress/hist.c` (rows 59-63)**\n`err_hist_wksp_alignment_and_size` (60/61/62/63) · `err_hist_maxsymbolvalue_toosmall` (59) · `err_entropy_pure_helpers`\n\n**`compress/huf_compress.c` (rows 64-80)**\n`err_huf_writectable_wksp_all` (64, 66, 67, 68, 69, 70) · `err_huf_buildctable_wksp_all` (64 again, 73, 74, 75) · `err_huf_initcstream_dstsize_toosmall` (76) · `err_huf_compress_repeat_guards` (77, 78, 79, 80 + guard ordering + all `flags`/`HUF_repeat` crossings) · `err_huf_misc_out_of_range`\n\nWitnesses found by brute force: row 69 needs a *power-of-two* alphabet (`msv=255`, flat CTable → uniform weights → `HUF_compressWeights` returns 1 \"rle\"); row 70 needs `msv ∈ {3,7,15,31,63,127}`; row 75 needs Fibonacci counts with `maxNbBits=13` (tree depth 13 passes `HUF_setMaxHeight`, then trips `maxNbBits > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX`).\n\n**`decompress/huf_decompress.c` (rows 268-304)**\n`err_huf_readdtable_x1` (272, 273) · `err_huf_readdtable_x2` (285, 286, 287) · `err_huf_decompress_1x_dctx_wksp` (298, 300, 301, 302) · `err_huf_decompress_4x_hufonly_wksp` (284, 299, 303, 304) · `err_huf_decompress_usingdtable_bodies` (274-277, 282, 288-291, 296) · `err_huf_decompress_fast_path` (268, 269, 270, 271, 283, 297) · `err_huf_decompress_fuzz`, `err_huf_decompress_wrappers_fuzz`\n\nRow 299 needed a purpose-built artifact: `HUF_selectDecoder` only picks X2 when `cSrcSize >= 96`, and `HUF_decompress4X2_DCtx_wksp`'s guard needs `cSrcSize <= hSize`, so a ≥96-byte *valid* table description is required. `HUF_writeCTable_wksp` never emits one that large (max observed 93), so `c_huf_big_desc()` constructs one (100 bytes) by FSE-coding a hand-built weight vector with a deliberately mismatched CTable, then validates it with `HUF_readStats`.\n\n## Sites I could NOT reach (with C evidence)\n\n- **Row 65** `HUF_compressWeights` `workspaceSize < sizeof(HUF_CompressWeightsWksp)` → GENERIC. Dead: the only caller is `HUF_writeCTable_wksp`, which passes `&wksp->wksp, sizeof(wksp->wksp)`; `wksp` is the first member of `HUF_WriteCTableWksp` and already 4-aligned, so `HUF_alignUpWorkspace` subtracts 0.\n- **Row 71** `HUF_readCTable` `tableLog > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX` → tableLog_tooLarge. Dead: `HUF_readStats` already returns `corruption_detected` for `tableLog > 12` (entropy_common.c L288).\n- **Rows 278 / 292** (`opStart4 > oend`). Dead: the body rejects `dstSize < 6` first, and `3*((n+3)/4) <= n` for every `n >= 6`.\n- **Rows 279/280/281 and 293/294/295** (`op1 > opStart2`, …). Only reachable, if at all, through the randomised corruption; the C annotates them \"should not be necessary : op# advance in lock step\". Covered by fuzzing, not asserted.\n\n## Documented-UB exclusions (stayed inside the domain; not \"fixed\" in Rust)\n\n1. `FSE_optimalTableLog` / `FSE_normalizeCount` with `total <= 1` or `maxSymbolValue == 0` → `ZSTD_highbit32(0)` (`assert(srcSize > 1)`, fse_compress.c L351/L362).\n2. `FSE_normalizeCount` with `(U32)total == 0` (e.g. `total == 2^32`) → `ZSTD_div64` divide-by-zero, SIGFPE in both libraries (verified).\n3. `HUF_buildCTable_wksp` with `maxNbBits ∈ 1..=4` and a deeper tree → `HUF_setMaxHeight` falls through to `huffNode[rankLast[13]]` where `rankLast[13] == 0xF0F0F0F0` (huf_compress.c L443). **Verified SIGSEGV in the C library.**\n4. `HUF_buildCTable_wksp` with `maxNbBits > HUF_TABLELOG_MAX+1` *and* a tree deeper than `maxNbBits` → `rankLast[targetNbBits-currentNbBits]` writes past `U32 rankLast[HUF_TABLELOG_MAX+2]` (L411/L420). Only shallow trees are probed with those values.\n5. `HUF_buildCTable_wksp` with an all-zero `count[]` (cardinality 0) → `nonNullRank == -1`, `HUF_buildCTableFromTree` walks off `huffNode`. **Verified SIGSEGV.** Replaced with uniform / single-symbol histograms.\n6. `HUF_selectDecoder(dstSize == 0, …)` → `cSrcSize * 16 / dstSize` divide-by-zero; only probed for `dstSize >= 1` (both public callers guard it).\n7. `HIST_count_simple` / `HIST_countFast` are documented \"unsafe : won't check if src contains values beyond count[] limit\" (hist.c L104/L172) — only called with data inside `[0, maxSymbolValue]`.\n\n## Rust source files fixed\n\n**None.** The Rust port matched the C ground truth (exact `size_t` sentinel, `ZSTD_getErrorCode`, all four `*_isError`/`*_getErrorName` accessors, every destination buffer, every out-parameter, every workspace and table buffer) on every one of the ~450 000 differential calls in this file. No `translation/src/**` change was required. Scratch probe programs used to brute-force the row-8 / row-55 / row-75 / row-299 witnesses were deleted; `Cargo.toml`, `tests/common/mod.rs` and all other test files are untouched."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":316758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":409,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01GsrJW4SDePc8qy5zJVbJm3","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"52ae2585-1381-4ebe-b86a-a6abd213dc4b","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:21:20.633Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C entropy error tests"}
