es the compressor never produces `noForwardProgress_*` (see below)\n`err_write_helpers_dst_too_small` | 145 `dstSize_tooSmall`, 146 `srcSize_wrong`, 148 `dstSize_tooSmall`; `ZSTD_getBlockSize`/`ZSTD_getSeqStore` state sweep\n`err_generate_sequences` | 135 `dstSize_tooSmall`, 138 `memory_allocation`, 140, 141 `sequenceProducer_failed`\n`err_compress_sequences_malformed` | 193, 194, 195, 198, 199, 200, 201, 202 `externalSequences_invalid` (13 mutation shapes × delimiters × validateSequences × repcodeResolution × maxBlockSize)\n`err_compress_sequences_and_literals` | 206, 207, 208, 209, 211, 214, 215 `externalSequences_invalid`; 216 `workSpace_tooSmall`; 217, 219 `frameParameter_unsupported`; 218 `parameter_unsupported`; 213 `cannotProduce_uncompressedBlock`; 204, 210, 212 `dstSize_tooSmall`\n`err_sequence_producer_failed` | 129, 130, 131 `sequenceProducer_failed`; 134, 193, 194, 197 `externalSequences_invalid` (11 producer modes × fallback × validateSequences × maxBlockSize × 6 sizes, one-shot + streaming, producer-call counts compared)\n`err_dictionary_corrupted_on_load` | 152–164 `dictionary_corrupted`, 165, 166, 181 `dictionary_wrong`, 110 `memory_allocation` (~110 corrupted dictionaries × 3 `dictContentType` × 2 `dictLoadMethod` × 4 entry points)\n`err_block_internals_dst_too_small` | 222, 223 `dstSize_tooSmall`; 224, 225, 227 `GENERIC`; 226, 228, 229 `dstSize_tooSmall` (direct `ZSTD_noCompressLiterals`, `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock`, `ZSTD_compressLiterals`, `ZSTD_buildCTable`, `ZSTD_encodeSequences`, `ZSTD_fseBitCost`)\n`err_superblock_dst_too_small` | 127, 128, 139, 142, 230 `dstSize_tooSmall`\n`err_estimate_size_nbworkers_generic` | 118, 119 `GENERIC`\n`err_compress_sequences_dst_too_small` | 205 `dstSize_tooSmall` (checksum)\n\nEvery comparison goes through `duo()`/dlsym and checks the error **code + name** (`eqcode`), the full `dst` (`eqbuf`), and `in.pos`/`out.pos`. `expect_code()` pins each row to its intended code rather than \"both failed\".\n\n## Sites I could NOT reach (with reasons)\n- **Row 182 `init_missing`** (`ZSTD_compressStream_generic` L6143) — unreachable: `ZSTD_compressStream_generic` is `static` and its only caller `ZSTD_compressStream2` always leaves `streamStage == zcss_load` before entering (either via `ZSTD_CCtx_init_compressStream2` or via the `stableInBuffer` early `return`). Legacy `flushStream`/`endStream`/`compressStream` all route through it. Driven anyway in `err_stage_wrong_and_init_missing` (before-init, after-end, after-error), where both libraries agree.\n- **Row 167 `stage_wrong`** (`ZSTD_writeEpilogue` L5350) — unreachable: `ZSTD_compressEnd_public` calls `ZSTD_compressContinue_internal` first, which rejects `ZSTDcs_created` at row 149.\n- **Row 171 `memory_allocation`** (`ZSTD_compress` `!cctx`) — compiled out: `ZSTD_COMPRESS_HEAPMODE` is 0 in this build, so `ZSTD_compress` uses a stack `ZSTD_CCtx ctxBody`.\n- **Row 203 `dstSize_tooSmall`** (empty-frame block header in `ZSTD_compressSequences_internal`) — unreachable: `ZSTD_writeFrameHeader` already demands `dstCapacity >= ZSTD_FRAMEHEADERSIZE_MAX (18)`, leaving ≥ 4 bytes.\n- **Row 239 `dstSize_tooSmall`** (`ZSTD_ldm_generateSequences_internal` \"out of sequence storage\") — defensive only: the caller always sizes `rawSeqStore.capacity` at `ZSTD_ldm_getMaxNbSeq()`, and `ldmState_t`'s layout is private so the function cannot be called directly.\n- **Rows 240–267** (`zstdmt_compress.c`) — out of scope for this file (`phase_c_misc::zstdmt`), and mostly unreachable in the non-MT build.\n- `noForwardProgress_destFull`, `noForwardProgress_inputEmpty`, `dstBuffer_null`, `dstBuffer_wrong` — **compression-side sites do not exist.** `grep -rn` over `c_src/src` shows all five producing lines live in `decompress/zstd_decompress.c` (L2359, L2360, L903, L916, L2049); the compressor has no stalled-call counter at all. `err_zero_progress_loops` still drives `out.size == out.pos` with data pending (40 iterations, stableOut 0/1), `in.size == in.pos` with `ZSTD_e_continue` (60 + 20 iterations, incl. `src == NULL`), and `compressStream`/`flushStream`/`endStream` into a zero-sized output (30 rounds) to prove both libraries spin identically and neither invents an error.\n\n## Rust source files fixed\n**None.** No C↔Rust divergence survived investigation. Two apparent mismatches turned out to be my own harness bugs and one was a transient concurrent edit:\n1. An out-of-bounds *read* triggered by my own test (see landmine #2 below) made the compressed output depend on heap history.\n2. My budgeted custom allocator originally used `std::alloc::alloc` (uninitialised). `ZSTD_customMalloc` hands the block straight to `ZSTD_cwksp_create`, so both libraries were being fed *different garbage*; switched to `alloc_zeroed`, which is the only valid way to compare.\n3. A ~2-minute window in which `translation/src/compress/zstd_compress_internal.rs` was being edited by a concurrent agent (mtime 06:15) produced a stale/half-built `libzstd.so` and 11 spurious failures; the next rebuild made all 21 tests pass.\n\n## NEW upstream landmines found (both libraries die identically — avoided + documented in the test file)\n1. **`ZSTD_compress2` + `ZSTD_c_targetCBlockSize` writes past `dst + dstCapacity`.** Reproduced with `targetCBlockSize = 1340`, class-4 (text-like) input of 1300 bytes, `dstCapacity = 792`: an unguarded heap destination is corrupted and the process dies with SIGSEGV on the *next* allocation. The C itself documents that the super-block writer is \"not bound by the standard `ZSTD_compressBound()`\" (`c_src/src/compress/zstd_compress.c:4470-4479`). `err_superblock_dst_too_small` gives both destinations a 64 KiB canary band on each side, compares the whole padded region (identical in C and Rust), and asserts the OOB write still reproduces so the defect stays visible.\n2. **`stableIn_notConsumed` survives `ZSTD_CCtx_reset`, causing an out-of-bounds read on the next session.** `ZSTD_compressStream_generic` parks unconsumed stable input in `zcs->stableIn_notConsumed` (`zstd_compress.c:6185`); `ZSTD_CCtx_reset` only touches `streamStage`/`pledgedSrcSizePlusOne` (`zstd_compress.c:1368-1381`). The next session executes `input->pos -= stableIn_notConsumed; ip -= stableIn_notConsumed;` (`zstd_compress.c:6120-6122`) on a fresh `pos == 0`, underflowing and reading *before* the caller's buffer (measured: `base - 8928` after a 140 000-byte `stableInBuffer` session). The guarding `assert` is compiled out because `DEBUGLEVEL` is unset. Because the two libraries are called in sequence, the C's own allocations can change that region between the calls, so the compressed output diverges purely from heap history. Every stable-buffer session in the tests now uses a brand-new `ZSTD_CCtx`. The same underflow is reachable within a single session by *shrinking* a stable input buffer after a sub-block-size `ZSTD_e_continue` call, which is why those two shapes are gated on `endOp == ZSTD_e_flush || first >= ZSTD_BLOCKSIZE_MAX`.\n3. `ZSTD_compressRleLiteralsBlock` dereferences `src[0]` unconditionally, so `srcSize == 0` with `src == NULL` segfaults (its header documents \"all bytes in `src` are identical\" and `dstCapacity >= 4` but not `srcSize > 0`). Guarded.\n4. `ZSTD_createCCtxParams_advanced` is **not exported** by the C build (it is `static`), so rows 89/90 are covered indirectly through `ZSTD_createCCtxParams`/`_advanced`'s NULL-return siblings rather than directly.\n\nAlso worth noting: `ZSTD_estimateCCtxSize_usingCCtxParams`'s `nbWorkers > 0` check (rows 118/119) is only reachable by writing the `ZSTD_CCtx_params::nbWorkers` field directly — `ZSTD_CCtxParams_setParameter` rejects non-zero `nbWorkers` with `parameter_unsupported` in this build and no `ZSTDMT_CCtxParam_setNbWorkers` is exported. `err_estimate_size_nbworkers_generic` re-declares the struct and **verifies its layout byte-for-byte** against a library-allocated, library-initialised object before touching the field (the check passes, so the 224-byte layout matches in both `.so`s)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":304,"cache_read_input_tokens":415664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":304,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01BaTYpCQhrTisraEQLqC9UL","session_id":"b0ef8e1e-2e1d-45e6-be23-c299770ecb9a","uuid":"df22d6c8-0f93-4bf3-b848-3eceb94c4848","timestamp":"2026-09-04T06:22:03.273Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C compress+streaming errors"}
